WEBVTT

01:58.995 --> 02:00.371
Good luck.

03:39.304 --> 03:42.223
Hi. I have an appointment with...

03:42.432 --> 03:43.975
...Emily Charlton?

03:44.851 --> 03:47.353
- Andrea Sachs?
- Yes?

03:47.520 --> 03:51.941
Great. Human Resources certainly has
an odd sense of humor. Follow me.

03:54.152 --> 03:56.988
Okay. So I was Miranda's
second assistant...

03:57.155 --> 04:00.158
...but her first recently got promoted,
and now I'm the first.

04:00.325 --> 04:02.535
- You're replacing yourself.
- Well, I am trying.

04:02.702 --> 04:05.204
Miranda sacked the last two girls
after a few weeks.

04:05.371 --> 04:07.165
We need someone
who can survive here.

04:07.332 --> 04:09.918
- Do you understand?
- Yeah, of course. Who's Miranda?

04:10.460 --> 04:13.212
Oh, my God. <i>I will</i> pretend
you did not just ask me that.

04:13.379 --> 04:16.966
She's the editor in chief of <i>Runway.</i>
Not to mention, a legend.

04:17.133 --> 04:20.345
Work a year for her and you can get
a job at any magazine you want.

04:20.553 --> 04:24.223
- A million girls would kill for this.
- It sounds like a great opportunity.

04:24.390 --> 04:26.434
I'd love to be considered.

04:28.144 --> 04:29.729
Andrea...

04:29.896 --> 04:34.734
...Runway is a fashion magazine,
so an interest in fashion is crucial.

04:34.943 --> 04:36.861
What makes you think
I'm not interested in fashion?

04:40.239 --> 04:41.616
Oh, my God.

04:41.783 --> 04:43.201
No,no,no!

04:44.619 --> 04:46.454
What's wrong?

04:50.708 --> 04:53.419
She's on her way. Tell everyone.

04:53.586 --> 04:55.838
She's not supposed to be here until 9.

04:55.922 --> 04:59.133
Her driver just text-messaged,
and her facialist ruptured a disk.

04:59.300 --> 05:01.469
God, these people.

05:01.636 --> 05:04.263
<i>- Who's that?
- That</i> I <i>can't even talk about.</i>

05:05.932 --> 05:08.351
All right, everyone. Gird your loinsl

05:09.727 --> 05:12.105
Did someone eat an onion bagel?

06:13.791 --> 06:15.918
Sorry, Miranda.

06:26.763 --> 06:28.681
Move it.

06:29.849 --> 06:33.269
I don't understand why
it's so difficult to confirm appointments.

06:33.436 --> 06:35.271
I'm so sorry. I actually did confirm--

06:35.438 --> 06:38.149
Details of your incompetence
do not interest me.

06:38.357 --> 06:42.111
Tell Simone I won't approve that girl
she sent me for the Brazilian layout.

06:42.320 --> 06:45.782
I asked for clean, athletic, smiley.
She sent dirty, tired and paunchy.

06:45.990 --> 06:47.909
R.S.V.P. "yes" to
the Michael Kors party.

06:48.076 --> 06:52.121
I want the driver to drop me off at 9:30
and pick me up at 9:45 sharp.

06:52.288 --> 06:55.750
Then call Natalie at Glorious Foods
and tell her "no" for the 40th time.

06:55.917 --> 06:59.212
I don't want dacquoise. I want tortes
filled with rhubarb compote.

06:59.378 --> 07:02.882
Call my ex and remind him the
parent-teacher conference is at Dalton.

07:03.091 --> 07:05.635
Then call my husband,
ask him to meet me for dinner...

07:05.843 --> 07:07.762
...at that place I went to
with Massimo.

07:07.929 --> 07:09.931
Tell Richard I saw
the pictures he sent...

07:10.098 --> 07:12.308
...for that feature
on female paratroopers...

07:12.475 --> 07:14.143
...and they're all so unattractive.

07:14.352 --> 07:16.354
Is it impossible to find a lovely...

07:16.521 --> 07:18.189
-...slender female paratrooper?
- No.

07:18.356 --> 07:19.941
- Am I reaching for the stars?
- No.

07:20.108 --> 07:21.400
Not really. Also...

07:21.567 --> 07:24.403
...I need to see all the things that
Nigel has pulled...

07:24.570 --> 07:26.239
...for Gwyneth's second cover try.

07:26.405 --> 07:29.242
I wonder if she's lost any of
that weight yet. Who is that?

07:29.325 --> 07:30.910
Nobody.

07:31.285 --> 07:34.288
Well, Human Resources sent her up
about the new assistant job.

07:34.455 --> 07:36.457
I was sort of
preinterviewing her for you.

07:36.624 --> 07:38.835
But she's hopeless
and totally wrong for this--

07:39.001 --> 07:41.003
Well, clearly, I have to
do that myself.

07:41.212 --> 07:44.048
The last two you sent me
were completely inadequate...

07:44.257 --> 07:46.092
...so send her in.

07:46.259 --> 07:47.552
That's all.

07:49.095 --> 07:50.221
Right.

07:53.850 --> 07:56.060
- She wants to see you.
- She does?

07:56.227 --> 07:58.020
Move.

08:01.023 --> 08:02.775
This is foul. Don't let her see it.

08:02.942 --> 08:04.944
- That's my-
- Go.

08:12.410 --> 08:13.536
Who are you?

08:14.537 --> 08:16.080
My name is Andy Sachs.

08:16.247 --> 08:19.292
I recently graduated from
Northwestern University.

08:19.500 --> 08:22.128
And what are you doing here?

08:22.336 --> 08:26.716
Well, I think I could do a good job
as your assistant.

08:27.300 --> 08:29.385
And...

08:30.887 --> 08:34.557
I came to New York to be a journalist,
and sent letters out everywhere...

08:34.724 --> 08:36.893
...and finally got a call
from Elias-Clarke...

08:37.101 --> 08:39.604
...and met with Sherry
up at Human Resources and-

08:40.688 --> 08:43.065
<i>Basically, it's this</i> or <i>Auto Universe.</i>

08:43.274 --> 08:47.403
- So you don't read <i>Runway?</i>
- No.

08:47.570 --> 08:53.201
- Before today, you'd never heard of me?
- No.

08:53.409 --> 08:56.454
And you have no style
or sense of fashion.

08:57.663 --> 08:59.290
Well...

09:00.291 --> 09:01.876
I think that depends on what you're...

09:01.959 --> 09:04.837
No, no. That wasn't a question.

09:08.466 --> 09:11.427
<i>I was editor</i> in <i>chief of
The Daily Northwestern.</i>

09:11.594 --> 09:16.307
I also won a national competition for
college journalists with my series...

09:16.390 --> 09:17.683
...on the Janitors' union...

09:17.767 --> 09:19.977
-...which exposed the exploitation of-
- That's all.

09:27.902 --> 09:31.572
Yeah, you know, okay.
You're right. I don't fit in here.

09:31.739 --> 09:37.245
I am not skinny or glamorous and
I don't know that much about fashion...

09:37.411 --> 09:39.830
...but I'm smart.

09:40.039 --> 09:43.042
- I learn fast and work very hard.
- I've got the exclusive on...

09:43.209 --> 09:44.502
...the Cavalli for Gwyneth.

09:44.669 --> 09:47.880
The problem is, with that huge
feathered headdress she's wearing...

09:48.047 --> 09:51.133
...she looks like she's working
the stage at the Golden Nugget.

09:51.300 --> 09:54.553
Thank you for your time.

09:54.762 --> 09:57.682
Who is that sad little person?

09:57.848 --> 10:00.184
Are we doing a before-and-after piece
I don't know about?

10:11.153 --> 10:12.488
Andrea.

10:17.451 --> 10:20.246
Wait. You got a job
at a fashion magazine?

10:20.413 --> 10:22.790
Well, what was it, a phone interview?

10:23.582 --> 10:26.043
<i>- Don't be a jerk.
- No, I'm just--</i>

10:26.210 --> 10:28.838
Miranda Priestly is famous
for being unpredictable.

10:29.046 --> 10:31.882
Okay, Doug. How is it that
you know who she is and I didn't?

10:32.091 --> 10:33.384
I'm actually a girl.

10:34.135 --> 10:36.053
That would explain so much.

10:36.262 --> 10:38.597
Look, seriously,
Miranda Priestly is a huge deal.

10:38.764 --> 10:40.725
A million girls would kill for that job.

10:40.933 --> 10:43.686
Yeah, great.
The thing is, I'm not one of them.

10:43.894 --> 10:46.230
Well, look.
You gotta start somewhere, right?

10:46.439 --> 10:48.316
I mean, look at this dump
Nate works in.

10:48.482 --> 10:51.152
I mean, come on.
Paper napkins? Hello?

10:51.360 --> 10:54.822
Yeah, and Lily, she works at
that gallery, doing... You know...

10:54.989 --> 10:58.242
Oh, I'm sorry.
What exactly is it that you do, anyway?

10:58.409 --> 11:01.495
Well, lucky for me,
I already have my dream job.

11:02.496 --> 11:05.291
- You're a corporate research analyst.
- Research analyst.

11:05.875 --> 11:07.793
- Oh, you're right. My job sucks.
- No.

11:07.960 --> 11:10.796
- It sucks. I don't- It's boring.
- It's all right. Breathe.

11:10.963 --> 11:12.214
- I'm trying.
- Take a drink.

11:12.423 --> 11:15.217
- I will have a drink.
- I would like to propose a toast.

11:15.426 --> 11:16.802
To jobs that pay the rent.

11:17.011 --> 11:20.723
- To jobs that pay the rent.
- Yes. To jobs that pay the rent.

11:20.931 --> 11:24.560
Oh, baby. You should see the way
these girls at <i>Runway</i> dress.

11:24.727 --> 11:26.520
I don't have a thing to wear to work.

11:26.687 --> 11:28.856
You'll be answering phones
and getting coffee.

11:29.023 --> 11:31.359
You need a ball gown for that?

11:31.525 --> 11:33.444
I think I might.

11:33.611 --> 11:37.198
Well, I happen to think
you look great always.

11:38.991 --> 11:41.369
I think you're full of it.

11:42.912 --> 11:44.288
- Hey. Come on.
- Yeah.

11:44.455 --> 11:46.957
Let's go. I can think of
something we can do...

11:47.041 --> 11:50.044
-...that doesn't require any clothing.
- Really?

11:58.010 --> 11:59.804
<i>- Hello?
- Andrea.</i>

12:00.012 --> 12:02.973
Miranda decided to kill
the autumn jacket story for September.

12:03.140 --> 12:05.351
She's putting up
the Sedona shoot from October.

12:05.518 --> 12:07.269
Come into the office this second.

12:07.478 --> 12:09.605
<i>- Pick up her coffee order on the way.
- Now'?</i>

12:09.814 --> 12:11.482
<i>Now, get a pen and write this down:</i>

12:11.690 --> 12:14.318
<i>I want one no-foam, skimmed latte...</i>

12:14.527 --> 12:17.446
...with an extra shot and
three coffees with room for milk.

12:17.655 --> 12:20.741
<i>Searing hot. And I mean hot.</i>

12:25.496 --> 12:27.373
<i>- Hello?
- Where are you?</i>

12:27.540 --> 12:29.375
I'm almost there. Yeah.

12:30.000 --> 12:31.669
Shoot

12:35.714 --> 12:38.717
Is there some reason
that my coffee isn't here?

12:38.926 --> 12:40.761
Has she died or something?

12:40.970 --> 12:43.931
No. God...

12:48.310 --> 12:50.771
Oh, about bloody time.

12:51.730 --> 12:55.651
I hope you know this is a very difficult
job for which you are totally wrong.

12:55.860 --> 12:58.320
If you mess up,
my head is on the chopping block.

12:58.779 --> 13:01.157
Now, hang that up.
Don't just fling it anywhere.

13:02.533 --> 13:05.494
- All right, where's the other layout?
- It's on its way.

13:05.703 --> 13:09.081
This is the first part of the collection,
which we talked about...

13:12.376 --> 13:15.004
Okay. First of all,
you and I answer the phones.

13:15.171 --> 13:18.257
The phone must be answered
every single time it rings.

13:18.466 --> 13:21.385
Calls roll to voice mail,
and she gets very upset.

13:21.594 --> 13:23.762
If I'm not here-— Andrea, Andrea.

13:23.846 --> 13:25.556
You are chained to that desk.

13:25.639 --> 13:27.850
Well, what if I need to...?

13:28.058 --> 13:30.394
What? No. One time,
an assistant left the desk...

13:30.561 --> 13:33.272
...because she sliced her hand open
with a letter opener.

13:33.481 --> 13:35.357
And Miranda missed Lagerfeld...

13:35.524 --> 13:38.486
...just before he boarded
a 17-hour flight to Australia.

13:38.652 --> 13:41.489
She now works at <i>TV</i> Guide.

13:42.573 --> 13:45.201
Man the desk at all times, got it.

13:48.579 --> 13:50.623
Miranda Priestly's office.

13:50.789 --> 13:52.082
No, she's not available.

13:52.291 --> 13:53.876
Who is--?

13:55.961 --> 13:57.922
Yes, <i>I will</i> tell her you called.

13:58.088 --> 13:59.465
Yet again.

14:01.258 --> 14:03.761
Remember,
you and I have totally different jobs.

14:03.969 --> 14:06.805
I mean, you get coffee
and you run errands.

14:06.972 --> 14:08.557
I am in charge of her schedule...

14:08.724 --> 14:11.519
...her appointments
and her expenses...

14:11.727 --> 14:16.023
...and most importantly, I get to go with
her to Paris for Fashion Week in the fall.

14:16.690 --> 14:19.485
I get to wear couture.
I go to all the shows and parties.

14:19.652 --> 14:22.154
I meet all of the designers.
It's divine.

14:23.531 --> 14:25.241
Okay, now, stay here.

14:25.449 --> 14:28.661
I'm going to the Art Department
to give them the Book.

14:28.827 --> 14:32.206
- The...?
- This is the Book.

14:32.373 --> 14:36.585
Now, it is a mockup of
everything in the current issue.

14:36.585 --> 14:40.421
We deliver it to Miranda's apartment
every night and she retu- Don't touch.

14:40.422 --> 14:42.925
She returns it to us in the morning
with her notes.

14:43.092 --> 14:46.303
Now, second assistant
<i>is</i> supposed to do this...

14:46.470 --> 14:50.307
...but Miranda is very private and
she does not like strangers in her house.

14:50.516 --> 14:53.477
So until she decides that
you're not a total psycho...

14:53.644 --> 14:55.479
...I get the lovely task of
waiting around for the Book.

14:58.399 --> 15:01.402
- Emily? What do I do if--?
- Deal with it.

15:06.574 --> 15:09.493
Hello, Mrs. Priestly's office.

15:10.160 --> 15:12.413
That's what I meant.
Miranda Priestly's office.

15:14.748 --> 15:18.544
You know, she is in a meeting.
Could I please take a message?

15:21.380 --> 15:22.923
<i>Okay-</i>

15:23.007 --> 15:25.050
Can you please spell "Gabbana"?

15:26.385 --> 15:28.012
Hello?

15:28.846 --> 15:30.389
I guess not.

15:31.890 --> 15:34.393
I guessed an eight and a half.

15:34.560 --> 15:37.271
Wow, that's very nice of you.

15:37.479 --> 15:40.024
But I don't think I need these.
Miranda hired me.

15:40.190 --> 15:42.610
- She knows what I look like.
- Do you?

15:46.864 --> 15:48.824
Emily.

15:48.991 --> 15:50.701
Emily?

15:51.577 --> 15:53.579
She means you.

15:56.790 --> 16:00.336
- We just cut on the bias and so what-
- No, that's not what I asked you.

16:00.502 --> 16:04.089
There you are, Emily. How many times
do I have to scream your name?

16:04.256 --> 16:05.466
Actually, it's Andy.

16:07.760 --> 16:11.930
My name is Andy.
Andrea, but everybody calls me Andy.

16:15.142 --> 16:19.605
- I need 10 or 15 skirts from Calvin Klein.
- Okay. What kind of skirts do you-?

16:19.772 --> 16:22.566
Please bore someone else
with your questions.

16:22.733 --> 16:26.278
And make sure we have Pier 59
at 8 a.m. tomorrow.

16:26.445 --> 16:30.199
Remind Jocelyn I need to see those
satchels that Marc is doing in the pony.

16:30.366 --> 16:33.494
And then tell Simone I'll take Jackie
if Maggie isn't available.

16:33.661 --> 16:35.245
Did Demarchelier confirm?

16:36.455 --> 16:38.874
- Did Demarcheli-—?
- Demarchelier. Did he--

16:39.041 --> 16:40.584
Get him on the phone.

16:41.710 --> 16:43.003
<i>Okay-</i>

16:44.588 --> 16:46.048
And, Emily...

16:46.507 --> 16:47.633
Yes?

16:59.103 --> 17:00.187
That's all.

17:01.188 --> 17:02.898
It's the cavalier disregard for...

17:11.824 --> 17:13.534
Do you have Demarchelier?

17:15.786 --> 17:17.371
Leave it.

17:21.375 --> 17:25.295
I have Miranda Priestly calling.
I have Patrick!

17:27.548 --> 17:30.634
She called me in there and then
she asked me about Pier 59.

17:30.801 --> 17:34.722
And there was something
about Simone, Frankie, someone else.

17:34.888 --> 17:38.016
And she needs skirts
from Calvin Klein.

17:38.434 --> 17:41.729
And there was something
about a pony.

17:42.187 --> 17:44.356
- Did she say which skirts?
- No.

17:44.523 --> 17:46.608
- Did she say what kind?
- I tried to ask her.

17:46.775 --> 17:49.069
You may never ask Miranda anything.

17:49.236 --> 17:53.282
Right. I will deal with all of this,
and you will go to Calvin Klein.

17:55.200 --> 17:56.702
- Me?
- Oh, I'm sorry.

17:56.869 --> 17:58.537
Do you have some prior commitment?

17:58.704 --> 18:01.081
Some hideous-skirt convention
you have to go to?

18:16.930 --> 18:18.265
<i>- Miranda?
- Are you there?</i>

18:18.432 --> 18:21.310
I'm about to walk in.
I'll call you as soon as I--

18:24.980 --> 18:26.315
<i>- Hello?
- While you're out...</i>

18:26.482 --> 18:30.277
<i>...Miranda needs you to go to Hermes
to pick up 25 scarves we ordered for her.</i>

18:30.444 --> 18:33.280
Cassidy forgot her homework at Dalton.
Pick that up.

18:33.447 --> 18:35.157
Miranda went out
to meet with Meisel.

18:35.324 --> 18:37.493
She'll want more Starbucks
when she gets back.

18:37.618 --> 18:40.704
- Hot Starbucks.
- Can you just repeat that first--? Hello?

18:45.959 --> 18:48.003
Oh, my God.

18:48.462 --> 18:50.756
What took you so long?
I have to pee.

18:50.923 --> 18:52.591
- You haven't peed since I left?
- No.

18:52.758 --> 18:55.260
Been manning the desk, haven't I?
I'm bursting.

19:00.265 --> 19:02.059
Oh, hi.

19:03.727 --> 19:07.064
- You do coat. Do the coat.
- Okay.

19:08.273 --> 19:11.527
Be prepared. The run-through
is at 12:30, and people are panicking.

19:11.693 --> 19:14.238
So the phone is going
to be ringing off the hook.

19:14.404 --> 19:16.031
The run-through. Right.

19:16.573 --> 19:19.701
Yes. Editors bring in options
for the shoot, and Miranda chooses.

19:19.868 --> 19:22.371
She chooses every single thing
in every single issue.

19:22.538 --> 19:25.332
It's a huge deal. I don't know
why you don't know that.

19:25.499 --> 19:27.334
- Okay, are you ready?
- Oh, hi, hi.

19:27.876 --> 19:30.712
Right, well, after the loo,
Serena and I are going to lunch.

19:30.879 --> 19:32.881
- This is her, the new me.
- Hi.

19:33.048 --> 19:35.092
- Told you.
- I thought you were kidding.

19:35.259 --> 19:36.969
No, quite serious, yeah.

19:37.135 --> 19:39.221
I get 20 minutes for lunch,
and you get 15.

19:39.388 --> 19:41.640
- When I come back, you can go.
- Okay.

19:41.807 --> 19:45.435
- What exactly is she wearing?
- Her grandmother's skirt.

19:58.448 --> 20:01.618
Corn chowder.
That's an interesting choice.

20:01.994 --> 20:06.456
You do know that cellulite is one of
the main ingredients in corn chowder?

20:11.670 --> 20:13.380
None of the girls here eat anything?

20:13.547 --> 20:17.551
Not since two became the new four
and zero became the new two.

20:17.718 --> 20:19.219
Well, I'm a six.

20:20.220 --> 20:21.805
Which is the new 14.

20:26.018 --> 20:27.728
- Shoot.
- Oh, never mind.

20:27.895 --> 20:31.773
I'm sure you have plenty more poly blend
where that came from.

20:32.733 --> 20:34.026
<i>Okay-</i>

20:34.276 --> 20:36.445
You think my clothes are hideous,
I get it.

20:36.528 --> 20:39.573
But, you know, I'm not
going to be in fashion forever...

20:39.740 --> 20:43.744
...so I don't see the point of changing
myself just because I have this job.

20:44.286 --> 20:45.621
Yes, that's true.

20:45.787 --> 20:49.541
That's what this multi-billion-dollar
industry is all about, anyway, isn't it?

20:49.708 --> 20:51.043
Inner beauty.

20:54.296 --> 20:55.839
Hello?

20:56.798 --> 20:58.258
Right. Come on.

20:58.425 --> 21:01.011
Miranda's pushed the run-through
up a half an hour.

21:01.219 --> 21:02.721
She's always 15 minutes early.

21:02.888 --> 21:04.681
- Which means...?
- You're already late.

21:04.848 --> 21:07.601
- Come. Excuse me.
- Shoot!

21:09.728 --> 21:12.189
- Mr. Ravitz.
- Nigel.

21:13.649 --> 21:16.276
- Issue going well?
- Oh, yes. Our best September ever.

21:16.443 --> 21:21.698
Great. Heard Miranda killed autumn
jackets and pulled up the Sedona shoot.

21:21.865 --> 21:25.786
- What's that costing me?
- About 300,000.

21:26.370 --> 21:28.830
Must have been some lousy jackets.

21:29.998 --> 21:31.875
- Irv Ravitz.
- Oh, I'm sorry.

21:32.042 --> 21:34.127
This is Andy Sachs,
Miranda's new assistant.

21:34.294 --> 21:38.840
Oh, congratulations, young lady.
A million girls would kill for that job.

21:39.007 --> 21:40.926
Bye-bye.

21:41.885 --> 21:44.805
Chairman of Elias-Clarke. Irv Ravitz.

21:44.972 --> 21:49.476
You know what they say:
Tiny man, huge ego.

21:52.437 --> 21:55.273
No. And I've seen all this before.

21:55.440 --> 21:58.276
Theyskens is trying to reinvent
the drop waist, so it's--

21:58.443 --> 22:01.405
- Where are all the other dresses?
- We have some right here.

22:01.571 --> 22:04.741
- Stand, watch and listen.
- I think it can be very interesting-

22:04.908 --> 22:05.951
No.

22:06.660 --> 22:09.162
No, I just--
It's just baffling to me.

22:09.246 --> 22:12.165
Why is it so impossible
to put together a decent run-through?

22:12.332 --> 22:15.377
You people have had
hours and hours to prepare.

22:15.544 --> 22:19.923
It's just so confusing to me.
Where are the advertisers?

22:20.090 --> 22:23.176
- We have some pieces from Banana--
- We need more, don't we? Oh.

22:23.343 --> 22:24.886
This is...

22:25.053 --> 22:28.140
- This might be-- What do you think of...?
- Yeah. You know me.

22:28.306 --> 22:31.810
Give me a full ballerina skirt
and a hint of saloon, and I'm on board.

22:31.977 --> 22:35.355
- But do you think it's too much like--?
- Like the Lacroix from July?

22:35.522 --> 22:38.275
I thought that, but no,
not with the right accessories.

22:38.442 --> 22:40.485
Where are the belts for this dress?

22:40.819 --> 22:43.071
Why is no one ready?

22:43.655 --> 22:47.617
Here. It's a tough call.
They're so different.

22:54.332 --> 22:55.667
Something funny?

22:59.212 --> 23:01.840
No. No, no, nothing's--

23:02.007 --> 23:06.136
You know, it's just that both those belts
look exactly the same to me.

23:06.303 --> 23:10.474
You know, I'm still
learning about this stuff and...

23:10.640 --> 23:13.351
"This stuff"?

23:14.186 --> 23:19.316
Oh, okay. I see. You think
this has nothing to do with you.

23:20.358 --> 23:22.778
You go to your closet...

23:22.944 --> 23:27.282
...and you select, I don't know,
that lumpy blue sweater, for instance...

23:27.449 --> 23:31.244
...because you're trying to tell the world
you take yourself too seriously...

23:31.411 --> 23:33.080
...to care about what you put on...

23:33.246 --> 23:36.458
...but what you don't know is that
that sweater is not just blue.

23:36.625 --> 23:40.921
It's not turquoise. It's not lapis.
It's actually cerulean.

23:41.088 --> 23:43.298
And you're also blithely
unaware of the fact...

23:43.465 --> 23:47.511
...that in 2002, Oscar de la Renta
did a collection of cerulean gowns...

23:47.677 --> 23:51.848
...and then it was Yves Saint Laurent
who showed Cerulean military jackets.

23:52.015 --> 23:53.475
I think we need a jacket here.

23:54.768 --> 23:58.814
Then cerulean quickly showed up in the
collections of eight different designers.

23:58.980 --> 24:02.109
And then it filtered down through
the department stores...

24:02.275 --> 24:06.446
...and then trickled on down
into some tragic Casual Corner...

24:06.613 --> 24:09.449
...where you, no doubt,
fished it out of some clearance bin.

24:09.616 --> 24:14.287
However, that blue represents
millions of dollars and countless jobs.

24:14.454 --> 24:17.666
And it's sort of comical how you think
that you've made a choice...

24:17.833 --> 24:20.127
...that exempts you
from the fashion industry...

24:20.293 --> 24:23.672
...when, in fact, you're wearing
a sweater that was selected for you...

24:23.839 --> 24:26.633
...by the people in this room...

24:26.716 --> 24:28.718
...from a pile of stuff.

24:29.761 --> 24:32.222
And then I said, no,
I couldn't see the difference...

24:32.389 --> 24:34.558
...between the two
absolutely identical belts.

24:34.724 --> 24:36.601
You should've seen
the look she gave me.

24:36.768 --> 24:39.938
I swear, I thought the flesh
was gonna melt off her face.

24:40.105 --> 24:41.481
It's not funny.

24:41.648 --> 24:45.694
She is not happy unless everyone around
her is panicked, nauseous or suicidal.

24:45.861 --> 24:48.822
And the clackers just worship her.

24:48.989 --> 24:50.824
- The who?
- They call them "clackers."

24:51.032 --> 24:53.702
The sound that their stilettos make
in the marble lobby.

24:53.869 --> 24:55.287
It's like:

24:57.247 --> 24:59.958
And they all act like
they're curing cancer or something.

25:00.125 --> 25:04.629
The amount of time and energy
that these people spend...

25:04.796 --> 25:08.258
...on these insignificant, minute details.
And for what?

25:08.425 --> 25:11.303
So that tomorrow they can spend
another $300,000...

25:11.469 --> 25:14.097
...reshooting something
that was fine to begin with...

25:14.264 --> 25:18.518
...to sell people things
they don't need. God!

25:20.478 --> 25:23.481
- I'm not even hungry anymore.
- What?

25:23.648 --> 25:27.277
- That is why those girls are so skinny.
- Oh, no, no, no. Give me that.

25:27.444 --> 25:30.280
There's, like, $8 of Jarlsberg in there.

25:31.489 --> 25:33.158
Know what?

25:34.075 --> 25:36.494
I just have to stick it out for a year.
One year.

25:36.661 --> 25:39.206
And then I can do
what I came to New York to do.

25:39.581 --> 25:41.875
But I can't let Miranda get to me.
I won't.

25:42.042 --> 25:44.377
Easy there, tiger.

25:46.630 --> 25:49.674
- Oh, good morning, Miranda.
- Get me Isaac.

25:51.384 --> 25:53.970
I don't see my breakfast here.
Where are my eggs?

25:54.137 --> 25:55.764
Excuse me!

25:55.931 --> 25:58.892
Pick up the Polaroids
from the lingerie shoot.

25:59.100 --> 26:02.520
Have the brakes checked on my car.

26:05.148 --> 26:08.235
Where is that piece of paper
I had in my hand yesterday morning?

26:08.902 --> 26:10.278
Girls need new surfboards...

26:10.445 --> 26:13.281
...or boogie boards
or something for spring break.

26:13.907 --> 26:16.618
- Hello?
- The twins also need flip-flops.

26:19.829 --> 26:21.873
Pick up my shoes from Blahnik...

26:22.040 --> 26:24.626
-...and then go get Patricia.
- Who's that?

26:24.793 --> 26:26.670
Good girl! Good girl! Good girl!

26:26.836 --> 26:30.382
Get me that little table that I like
at that store on Madison.

26:30.548 --> 26:34.511
Get us a reservation for dinner tonight
at that place that got the good review.

26:34.678 --> 26:37.138
- Notes delivered today.
Where is everyone?

26:37.305 --> 26:40.433
Why is no one working?
- East Side.

26:41.601 --> 26:44.020
Get me Demarchelier.

26:50.235 --> 26:53.488
I have Miranda Priestly
calling for-- Okay.

26:54.698 --> 26:56.825
I have Patrick.

27:02.580 --> 27:04.499
Thank God it's Friday, right?

27:04.666 --> 27:08.837
At least Miranda will be in Miami, so we
don't have to be on call this weekend.

27:09.004 --> 27:11.006
You know, my dad's coming in
from Ohio.

27:11.172 --> 27:14.467
Yeah, we're gonna go out to dinner
and maybe see Chicago.

27:14.634 --> 27:16.344
You doing anything fun this weekend?

27:17.178 --> 27:18.179
Yes.

27:22.350 --> 27:24.311
Yeah, Nate said it was great.

27:24.477 --> 27:28.148
He actually- He applied here but they
wanted someone with more experience.

27:28.315 --> 27:30.275
- Here.
- What's this?

27:30.442 --> 27:32.944
I don't want you
to get behind on your rent.

27:33.111 --> 27:36.156
- Dad? How did you...?
- It's...

27:37.073 --> 27:39.200
I'm gonna kill Mom.

27:40.618 --> 27:42.203
Thank you.

27:46.624 --> 27:49.377
- It's really good to see you.
- You too, honey.

27:50.295 --> 27:54.716
So do you wanna start grilling me now,
or should we wait till after dinner?

27:54.883 --> 27:57.802
I thought I'd let you
at least enjoy the breadbasket first.

27:57.969 --> 27:59.929
No, no, no, that's okay.
Go right ahead.

28:00.555 --> 28:02.307
We're just a little worried, honey.

28:02.474 --> 28:05.018
We get e-mails from you
at your office at 2 a.m.

28:05.185 --> 28:07.729
Your pay is terrible.
You don't get to write anything.

28:07.896 --> 28:09.898
Hey, that's not fair.

28:10.273 --> 28:12.359
I wrote those e-mails.

28:12.442 --> 28:15.904
I'm trying to understand why someone
who got accepted to Stanford Law...

28:16.071 --> 28:19.908
...turns it down to be a journalist,
and now you're not even doing that.

28:20.075 --> 28:23.036
Dad, you have to trust me.

28:23.203 --> 28:25.997
Being Miranda's assistant
opens a lot of doors.

28:26.831 --> 28:29.626
Emily is going to Paris with Miranda
in a few months...

28:29.793 --> 28:33.588
...and she's gonna meet editors and
writers from every important magazine...

28:33.755 --> 28:35.632
...and in a year, that could be me.

28:36.758 --> 28:42.013
All right? Dad, I swear,
this is my break. This is my--

28:42.180 --> 28:44.557
My chance. This is...

28:44.808 --> 28:46.476
_..my boss.

28:48.395 --> 28:50.855
I'm sorry, Dad. I have to take this.

28:51.022 --> 28:55.193
- Hello, Miranda?
- My flight has been cancelled.

28:55.360 --> 28:58.822
There's some absurd weather problem.
I need to get home tonight.

28:58.988 --> 29:01.491
The twins have a recital
tomorrow morning at school.

29:01.658 --> 29:03.076
<i>- What?</i>
- At school.

29:03.243 --> 29:05.912
<i>- Absolutely. Let me see what I can do.
- Good.</i>

29:06.079 --> 29:08.873
Hi. I know this is totally last minute...

29:09.040 --> 29:12.293
...but I was hoping that you could
maybe get a flight for my boss...

29:12.460 --> 29:14.754
...from Miami to New York tonight?

29:16.172 --> 29:19.092
- Yeah. Yeah, any kind ofjet.
- Right here. Thank you.

29:19.259 --> 29:21.136
- From Miami to New York.
- Thank you.

29:21.302 --> 29:23.388
Yes, I need it tonight. I need it--

29:23.555 --> 29:26.433
- I thought you were going out-
- No. It's over here, honey.

29:26.599 --> 29:31.271
Hi, I'm trying to get a flight tonight,
for tonight, from Miami to New York.

29:31.438 --> 29:34.399
Yes, I know there's a hurricane.

29:34.983 --> 29:37.527
Nothing is flying out?
What do you mean, nothing?

29:37.694 --> 29:40.113
It's for Miranda Priestly.
She's a client of yours.

29:40.280 --> 29:42.282
She's flown with you before.
Yes, yes, hi.

29:42.449 --> 29:45.326
I need a jet tonight
from Miami to New York.

29:45.493 --> 29:47.704
- Yeah. Sorry, hold on.
- What?

29:47.871 --> 29:49.372
Hello? Miranda, hi.

29:49.539 --> 29:53.042
I'm trying to get a flight, but no one
is flying, because of the weather.

29:53.209 --> 29:57.005
Please. It's just,
I don't know, drizzling.

29:57.172 --> 29:58.882
Well, someone must be getting out.

29:59.048 --> 30:00.842
Call Donatella. Get her jet.

30:01.009 --> 30:03.386
<i>Call everybody else that we know
that has a jet.</i>

30:03.553 --> 30:06.139
<i>Call every-- This is your respons-
This is your job.</i>

30:06.306 --> 30:08.183
Get me home.

30:08.558 --> 30:11.060
Oh, my God.
She's going to murder me.

30:11.144 --> 30:14.314
What does she want you to do,
have the National Guard airlift her?

30:14.481 --> 30:16.858
Of course not. Could I do that?

30:17.275 --> 30:18.985
Come on. Come on.

30:20.778 --> 30:23.406
The girls' recital
was absolutely wonderful.

30:23.573 --> 30:25.825
They played Rachmaninoff.
Everyone loved it.

30:25.992 --> 30:32.457
Everyone except me,
because, sadly, I was not there.

30:33.458 --> 30:36.961
- Miranda, I'm so sorry.
- Do you know why I hired you?

30:37.712 --> 30:40.131
I always hire the same girl.

30:40.298 --> 30:45.303
Stylish, slender, of course,
worships the magazine.

30:45.470 --> 30:48.681
But so often, they turn out to be...

30:49.098 --> 30:51.601
...I don't know, disappointing. And...

30:53.061 --> 30:54.395
...stupid.

30:55.438 --> 30:59.484
So you,
with that impressive résumé...

30:59.651 --> 31:02.612
...and the big speech
about your so-called work ethic...

31:02.779 --> 31:05.698
...I thought you would be different.

31:06.449 --> 31:11.037
I said to myself, "Go ahead.
Take a chance.

31:11.204 --> 31:14.457
Hire the smart fat girl."

31:16.417 --> 31:18.461
I had hope.

31:18.628 --> 31:20.713
My God, I live on it.

31:21.714 --> 31:25.593
Anyway, you ended up
disappointing me more than...

31:26.594 --> 31:29.013
More than any
of the other silly girls.

31:33.268 --> 31:35.603
I really did everything I could think of.

31:35.812 --> 31:38.064
That's all.

31:47.490 --> 31:49.909
Excuse me, where do you
think you're going?

32:09.178 --> 32:11.556
She hates me, Nigel.

32:12.515 --> 32:16.853
And that's my problem because...
Oh, wait, no. It's not my problem.

32:17.061 --> 32:20.398
I don't know what else I can do
because if I do something right...

32:20.607 --> 32:23.234
...it's unacknowledged.
She doesn't even say thank you.

32:23.401 --> 32:28.448
But if I do something wrong,
she is vicious.

32:28.656 --> 32:30.575
So quit.

32:30.992 --> 32:32.410
What?

32:32.619 --> 32:34.412
- Quit.
- Qui--

32:34.621 --> 32:37.081
I can get a girl to take
your job in five minutes.

32:37.290 --> 32:39.042
One who really wants it.

32:39.250 --> 32:41.586
But no, I don't wanna quit.
That's not fair.

32:41.794 --> 32:44.297
But I-- You know,
I'm just saying that...

32:44.505 --> 32:48.676
...I would just like a little credit for
the fact that I'm killing myself trying.

32:48.885 --> 32:52.722
Andy, be serious. You are not trying.

32:53.598 --> 32:56.601
You are whining.

32:57.560 --> 32:59.395
What do you want me
to say to you, huh?

32:59.896 --> 33:02.899
Do you want me to say, "Poor you,
Miranda's picking on you...

33:03.107 --> 33:05.151
---POOF you, poor Andy"?

33:05.360 --> 33:09.530
Wake up, six. She's just doing her job.

33:09.739 --> 33:11.282
You are working at the place...

33:11.491 --> 33:14.494
...that published some of
the greatest artists of the century:

33:14.702 --> 33:17.914
Halston, Lagerfeld, de la Renta.

33:18.122 --> 33:23.336
And what they did, what they created,
was greater than art.

33:23.544 --> 33:25.380
Because you live your life in it.

33:26.923 --> 33:30.802
Well, not you, obviously.
But some people.

33:31.010 --> 33:35.807
You think this is just a magazine?
This is not just a magazine.

33:36.015 --> 33:39.852
This is a shining beacon of hope for...

33:40.728 --> 33:41.979
Oh, I don't know.

33:42.438 --> 33:45.566
Let's say, a young boy growing up
in Rhode Island with six brothers...

33:45.650 --> 33:48.820
...pretending to go to soccer when he
was going to sewing class...

33:48.986 --> 33:52.156
...and reading <i>Runway</i> under the covers
at night with a flashlight.

33:52.365 --> 33:56.077
You have no idea how many legends
have walked these halls, and worse...

33:56.285 --> 33:58.871
...you don't care. Because this place...

33:59.080 --> 34:04.001
...where so many people would die
to work, you only deign to work.

34:04.419 --> 34:07.755
And you want to know why she
doesn't kiss you on the forehead...

34:07.964 --> 34:12.260
...and give you a gold star on your
homework at the end of the day.

34:14.053 --> 34:16.472
Wake up, sweetheart.

34:23.020 --> 34:25.398
Okay, so I'm screwing it up.

34:26.482 --> 34:31.070
I mean, I don't want to, I just wish
that I knew what I could do...

34:37.076 --> 34:40.246
Nigel? Nigel, Nigel.

34:42.749 --> 34:43.499
No.

34:44.625 --> 34:46.961
I don't know what
you expect me to do.

34:47.044 --> 34:50.506
There's nothing in this closet that'll
fit a size six, I can guarantee you.

34:53.593 --> 34:56.554
These are all sample sizes,
two and four.

34:57.221 --> 34:59.182
All right, we're doing this for you...

34:59.390 --> 35:01.225
- And--
- A poncho?

35:01.601 --> 35:03.895
You'll take what I give you
and you'll like it.

35:04.103 --> 35:06.731
We're doing this Dolce for you.

35:07.148 --> 35:09.942
And shoes...

35:10.151 --> 35:11.569
Jimmy Choos.

35:12.820 --> 35:14.989
Manolo Blahnik.

35:15.907 --> 35:18.951
Nancy Gonzalez, love that.

35:19.160 --> 35:21.412
Okay, Narciso Rodriguez.
This we love.

35:22.705 --> 35:24.999
- It might fit. It might.
- What?

35:25.208 --> 35:28.169
Okay, now Chanel. You're in
desperate need of Chanel.

35:28.336 --> 35:31.005
Shall we? We have to get
to the Beauty Department...

35:31.172 --> 35:34.133
...and God knows how long
that's going to take.

35:34.300 --> 35:37.887
I mean, I have no idea
why Miranda hired her.

35:38.095 --> 35:40.723
Me neither. We were
in the Beauty Department...

35:40.932 --> 35:43.851
...and she held up the Shu Uemura
eyelash curler and said:

35:44.060 --> 35:45.812
"What is this?"

35:46.938 --> 35:49.607
I mean, I just knew from
the moment I saw her...

35:49.816 --> 35:52.568
...she was going to be
a complete and utter disas-

36:03.579 --> 36:04.997
Miranda Priestly's office.

36:05.706 --> 36:08.501
No, actually, she's not available
but I'll leave word.

36:08.709 --> 36:10.753
Okay, thanks. Bye.

36:12.588 --> 36:14.382
How did--?

36:15.883 --> 36:18.010
- Are you wearing the Ch--
- The Chanel boots?

36:18.219 --> 36:20.721
Yeah, I am.

36:21.639 --> 36:23.516
You look good.

36:25.810 --> 36:27.687
What?

36:28.604 --> 36:30.982
- She does.
- Oh, shut up, Serena.

36:33.860 --> 36:36.612
- See you guys tomorrow.
- Good night, man. Take it easy.

36:36.821 --> 36:39.031
Take care of that finger, huh?

36:56.215 --> 36:57.758
So...

36:59.093 --> 37:00.928
...what do you think?

37:02.972 --> 37:06.392
I think we better get out of here
before my girlfriend sees me.

37:53.981 --> 37:56.776
The gowns are fabulous, Ralph.

37:57.818 --> 38:00.071
We're gonna use the burgundy...

38:05.034 --> 38:07.244
...for the cover try...

38:11.415 --> 38:14.669
So we spent a whole semester
on potatoes alone.

38:14.877 --> 38:17.254
Take the fry and squeeze it.
See how firm that is?

38:17.421 --> 38:19.632
Hey. Oh, I'm so sorry I'm late.

38:20.466 --> 38:23.219
There was a crisis
in the Accessories Department.

38:23.344 --> 38:26.389
- I needed to find a python headband.
- Python's hot right now.

38:27.056 --> 38:30.267
I have exciting presents for all of you.

38:30.351 --> 38:32.520
Are you ready?

38:33.354 --> 38:36.607
- What is that?
- It's a Bang and Olufsen phone.

38:36.816 --> 38:39.276
Charlie Rose sent it to Miranda
for her birthday.

38:39.485 --> 38:42.697
I looked it up online.
It's eleven hundred dollars.

38:42.905 --> 38:44.490
- What?
- Yep.

38:44.699 --> 38:47.868
And I have some products.
Mason Pearson hairbrushes.

38:48.077 --> 38:49.370
A little Clinique.

38:49.996 --> 38:52.331
Oh, damn it, I love your job.

38:52.581 --> 38:54.041
Oh, one more...

38:54.125 --> 38:55.960
...little thing.

38:57.169 --> 38:59.672
- Do you want it? You want-- Oh.
- Gimme, gimme, gimme!

38:59.839 --> 39:01.716
- I think she likes it.
- Oh, my God!

39:01.924 --> 39:04.844
This is the new Marc Jacobs!
This is sold out everywhere.

39:05.011 --> 39:08.180
- Where did you get this?
- Miranda didn't want it, so...

39:08.389 --> 39:13.269
Oh, no, no, no. This bag is, like,
$1900. I cannot take this from you.

39:13.644 --> 39:16.731
- Yeah, you can.
- Why do women need so many bags?

39:16.939 --> 39:19.358
- Shut up.
- You have one, you put all yourjunk...

39:19.567 --> 39:22.903
-...in it, and that's it, you're done.
- Fashion is not about utility.

39:23.070 --> 39:25.656
An accessory is merely
a piece of iconography...

39:25.823 --> 39:27.867
...used to express individual identity.

39:28.909 --> 39:31.370
- And it's pretty.
- That too.

39:31.579 --> 39:35.124
It turns out that there is more
to <i>Runway</i> than just fancy purses.

39:35.624 --> 39:39.211
Look. Here is an essay by Jay Mclnerney,
a piece by Joan Didion...

39:39.420 --> 39:42.465
...even an interview with
Christiane Amanpour.

39:42.673 --> 39:44.383
Someone's been
drinking the Kool-Aid.

39:44.592 --> 39:46.677
What are you--?

39:47.762 --> 39:48.888
- Nate.
- I got it.

39:49.055 --> 39:51.432
-It's- Yep, the dragon lady.
- Let me talk to her.

39:51.599 --> 39:55.561
- No. Okay, I need that. Lily, no, no, no!
- Tell her to get her own scrambled eggs.

39:55.728 --> 40:01.317
It's gonna answer it! It's gonna
answer it! Gimme the phone! The phone.

40:03.360 --> 40:05.654
Hi, Miranda.

40:07.198 --> 40:08.574
Absolutely.

40:10.409 --> 40:11.786
I'm leaving right now.

40:12.745 --> 40:16.916
You know, you guys didn't
have to be such assholes.

40:48.781 --> 40:52.701
Excuse me.
I'm looking for James Holt.

40:54.036 --> 40:56.622
- That's him right there.
- Oh, oh, thanks.

40:56.831 --> 40:58.249
No problem.

40:58.457 --> 41:01.043
I put my stuff out there
and I pray they approve.

41:01.836 --> 41:06.090
Excuse me. I'm Andy.
I'm picking up for Miranda Priestly.

41:06.298 --> 41:08.843
Oh, yes. You must be
the new Emily.

41:09.051 --> 41:11.387
- Oh, yeah.
- Nice to meet you.

41:11.595 --> 41:15.182
Oh, let me see that bag.
Very, very nice.

41:15.391 --> 41:19.186
Distressed, studded leather, pieced by
hand, finished with a metallic fringe.

41:19.353 --> 41:21.814
Very nice, indeed.
Who made that fantastic thing?

41:23.065 --> 41:24.692
You.

41:31.866 --> 41:35.119
Here we go. It's a sketch
of Miranda's dress for the benefit.

41:35.119 --> 41:38.580
Also the centerpiece of my spring
collection. Top-secret stuff.

41:38.581 --> 41:40.666
<i>- I'll</i> guard it with my life.
- Please do.

41:40.875 --> 41:45.421
Come on. You're working for Miranda,
you must be in need of hard liquor.

41:48.090 --> 41:49.925
Excuse us, girls.

41:50.134 --> 41:52.094
She'll have the punch.

41:55.806 --> 41:58.893
It's deadly. Have fun.

42:03.147 --> 42:05.399
He's right, you know.

42:06.150 --> 42:07.484
The punch.

42:07.693 --> 42:11.030
I drank it at his last party. I woke
up in Hoboken wearing nothing...

42:11.197 --> 42:13.616
...but a poncho and a cowboy hat.

42:13.824 --> 42:16.118
Well.

42:16.327 --> 42:18.370
Wise.

42:18.579 --> 42:21.582
- Hi.
- Christian Thompson.

42:22.833 --> 42:25.336
Christian Thompson? You're kidding.

42:25.544 --> 42:28.964
No, you're- You write for, like,
every magazine I love.

42:29.173 --> 42:32.551
I reviewed your collection of essays
for my college newspaper.

42:32.760 --> 42:35.596
Did you mention my good looks
and my killer charm?

42:35.804 --> 42:37.932
- No, but--
- What do you do?

42:38.641 --> 42:44.188
Oh, well... I wanna work for somewhere
like The New Yorker or <i>Vanity Fair.</i>

42:44.396 --> 42:46.649
- I am a writer too.
- Is that right?

42:46.857 --> 42:48.859
I should read your stuff. Send it over.

42:49.068 --> 42:51.111
Yeah?

42:51.320 --> 42:53.489
That would-- Thank you.
That would be great.

42:55.282 --> 42:58.577
Actually, right now, I'm working
as Miranda Priestly's assistant.

42:58.786 --> 43:02.957
Oh, you're kidding.
Well, that's too bad. That's- Whoa.

43:03.499 --> 43:05.125
You'll never survive Miranda.

43:06.877 --> 43:10.130
- Excuse me?
- Well, you seem nice, smart.

43:10.547 --> 43:12.341
You can't do that job.

43:14.802 --> 43:16.220
Gotta go.

43:16.428 --> 43:21.976
Okay. Well, it was very, very nice
to meet you, Miranda girl.

43:37.074 --> 43:38.701
Emily?

43:46.917 --> 43:50.087
Call James Holt's office. Tell them
I wanna move the preview up.

43:50.254 --> 43:54.174
Today at 12:30. Tell everybody else.
Be ready to leave in half an hour.

43:54.842 --> 43:56.927
<i>But we're not expected
until Tuesday.</i>

43:57.136 --> 43:59.471
- Did she say why?
- Yes. She explained...

43:59.555 --> 44:03.017
...every detail of her decision-making.
Then we brushed each other's hair...

44:03.100 --> 44:05.644
-...and gabbed about American <i>Idol.</i>
- I see your point.

44:06.645 --> 44:09.231
<i>- What's a preview, anyway?
- Good</i> morning, <i>Miranda.</i>

44:09.440 --> 44:13.610
<i>Miranda insists on seeing the designer's
collections before they show them.</i>

44:13.819 --> 44:15.446
- Great to see you again.
- Hello.

44:15.779 --> 44:18.532
<i>- And she tells them what she thinks?
- In her way.</i>

44:18.741 --> 44:22.119
This season really began for me
with a meditation...

44:22.328 --> 44:24.872
...on the intersection
between East and West.

44:25.080 --> 44:28.459
<i>There's a scale. One nod is good.
Two nods, very good.</i>

44:29.043 --> 44:32.713
<i>There's only been one actual smile on
record, and that was Tom Ford in 2001.</i>

44:32.921 --> 44:34.214
An obi belt.

44:34.298 --> 44:36.342
<i>If she doesn't like it,
she shakes her head.</i>

44:37.217 --> 44:40.846
This is the dress we have designed
specifically and exclusively for you.

44:41.055 --> 44:43.682
<i>Then, of course,
there's the pursing of the lips.</i>

44:43.891 --> 44:45.768
<i>Which means...?</i>

44:50.230 --> 44:51.815
<i>Catastrophe.</i>

44:52.900 --> 44:55.152
Just- Just go.

44:55.944 --> 44:58.364
- I know.
- I just don't understand. I'm appalled.

44:58.572 --> 45:01.533
- Appalled. <i>I'll</i> talk to him.
- You deal with it.

45:01.825 --> 45:05.496
So because she pursed her lips,
he's gonna change his entire collection?

45:05.704 --> 45:07.498
You still don't get it, do you?

45:07.706 --> 45:10.918
Her opinion is the only one
that matters.

45:12.920 --> 45:16.006
- Call my husband and confirm dinner-
- At Pastis? Done.

45:16.173 --> 45:17.883
And I'll need a change of clothes.

45:18.092 --> 45:21.595
Well, I've already messengered
your outfit over to the shoot.

45:23.180 --> 45:27.726
Fine. And Andrea, I would like you
to deliver the Book to my home tonight.

45:27.935 --> 45:30.354
Have Emily give you the key.

45:32.231 --> 45:35.818
- Guard this with your life.
- Of course.

45:36.693 --> 45:40.739
You know, if I can deliver the Book, that
means I must've done something right.

45:40.948 --> 45:42.741
I'm not a psycho.

45:42.950 --> 45:44.701
And, you know she called me Andrea?

45:44.910 --> 45:47.913
I mean, she didn't call me Emily.
Isn't that great?

45:48.122 --> 45:50.207
Yeah, whoopee.

45:52.918 --> 45:57.047
Now, it's very important that you do
exactly what I'm about to tell you.

45:57.256 --> 45:59.091
Oh, okay.

45:59.299 --> 46:02.344
<i>The Book is assembled by 10, 10:30...</i>

46:02.553 --> 46:05.514
<i>...and you must wait around for it
until then.</i>

46:06.098 --> 46:09.309
You will be delivering Miranda's
dry-cleaning with the Book.

46:11.937 --> 46:15.607
<i>Now, the car will take you
straight to Miranda's townhouse.</i>

46:15.816 --> 46:18.110
<i>You let yourself in.</i>

46:20.237 --> 46:25.868
Andrea. You do not talk to anyone.
You do not look at anyone.

46:26.076 --> 46:31.123
This is of the utmost importance. You
must be invisible. Do you understand?

46:31.331 --> 46:34.543
<i>You open the door
and you walk across the foyer.</i>

46:34.751 --> 46:39.840
<i>You hang the dry-cleaning in the closet
across from the staircase.</i>

46:47.014 --> 46:49.933
<i>And you leave the Book
on the table with the flowers.</i>

46:57.107 --> 47:00.068
- Shit.
- It's that door to the left.

47:04.907 --> 47:06.700
<i>Okay-</i>

47:12.915 --> 47:14.958
Thank you.

47:16.460 --> 47:17.961
You can give the Book to us.

47:19.046 --> 47:21.673
- Which...? Which table?
- It's okay. Come on up.

47:21.840 --> 47:24.218
- No, I can't. I can't.
- What? It's okay. Come on.

47:24.426 --> 47:27.763
- Yeah, come on. It's okay.
- Please stop talking.

47:27.971 --> 47:31.099
Or you could bring the Book upstairs.
Emily does it all the time.

47:31.266 --> 47:35.521
She does? Right. She does.
All the time.

47:35.729 --> 47:38.690
Yeah? Okay.

47:45.489 --> 47:48.534
What did you expect me to do,
walk out in the middle of a shoot?

47:48.700 --> 47:51.078
I rushed out of an
investment committee meeting.

47:51.286 --> 47:53.830
- And I sat there waiting.
- I told you cell phones...

47:54.039 --> 47:55.541
...didn't work. No signals.

47:55.707 --> 47:58.043
I knew everyone in the restaurant
was thinking:

47:58.210 --> 48:01.213
"There he is, waiting for her again."

48:26.029 --> 48:27.406
Okay, okay.

48:27.573 --> 48:30.242
Okay, okay. It really wasn't
that big a deal. I promise.

48:30.409 --> 48:32.828
The twins said hello,
I said hello back and then...

48:32.995 --> 48:34.788
...I went up to give her the Book...

48:35.289 --> 48:37.416
You went upstairs?
You went upstairs. My God.

48:37.583 --> 48:41.086
Why didn't you just climb into bed
with her and ask for a bedtime story?

48:41.295 --> 48:44.172
Okay. Okay.
I made a mistake. I know.

48:44.381 --> 48:45.966
Andrea, you don't understand.

48:46.174 --> 48:49.344
If you get fired, that might
jeopardize Paris. If that happens...

48:49.511 --> 48:52.347
...I'll search every Blimpie's
in the tristate area for you.

48:52.514 --> 48:54.975
Hold on. She's gonna fire me?

48:55.142 --> 48:58.770
I don't know. She's not happy.

48:58.937 --> 49:00.314
Andrea.

49:10.907 --> 49:14.077
- Miranda, about last night, I'm--
- I need the <i>Harry</i> Potter book...

49:14.244 --> 49:15.495
...for the twins.

49:16.079 --> 49:18.707
Okay. Okay, <i>I'll</i> go down
to Barnes and Noble right now.

49:18.874 --> 49:22.753
Did you fall down and smack
your little head on the pavement?

49:24.713 --> 49:27.716
- Not that I can recall.
- We have all the published books.

49:27.883 --> 49:30.552
The twins want to know
what happens next.

49:32.012 --> 49:34.139
You want the unpublished manuscript?

49:34.306 --> 49:37.684
We know everyone in publishing.
It shouldn't be a problem, should it?

49:37.851 --> 49:40.354
And you can do anything, right?

49:48.278 --> 49:49.738
Yes, Bobbsey?

49:49.905 --> 49:53.533
I know, baby. Mommy's working
very hard to get it for you.

49:53.742 --> 49:57.371
She doesn't get it. You know, I could
call fricking J. K. Rowling herself.

49:57.537 --> 49:59.456
I'm not gonna get a copy
of that book.

49:59.665 --> 50:04.336
My girls leave for their grandmother's
at 4 so the book better be here by 3.

50:04.544 --> 50:07.339
- Of course.
- And I would like my steak here...

50:07.547 --> 50:09.091
...in 15 minutes.

50:09.299 --> 50:11.259
No problem.

50:11.968 --> 50:15.931
Okay. I have four hours
to get the impossible manuscript.

50:16.098 --> 50:18.433
Smith and Wollensky's
doesn't open until 11:30.

50:18.600 --> 50:20.227
How am I gonna get the steak?

50:20.394 --> 50:24.314
Okay. <i>I will</i> be back
in 15 minutes. Wish me luck.

50:24.523 --> 50:25.691
No, shan't.

50:25.899 --> 50:29.778
Yes, yes, yes, I've been on hold.
Well, it's for Miranda Priestly.

50:29.945 --> 50:31.363
It's very important.

50:31.530 --> 50:35.742
Yes, I know. I know it's impossible
to get, but, well, I was wondering...

50:35.909 --> 50:39.871
...if you could make the impossible
possible, if that's at all possible?

50:40.080 --> 50:43.333
Yes, I'm calling about
the <i>Harry</i> Potter manuscript.

50:44.167 --> 50:46.378
No. Unpublished.

50:46.795 --> 50:50.882
Not a chance? Could you tell her
that it's for Miranda Priestly?

50:51.091 --> 50:53.093
Because I think it makes a difference.

50:58.432 --> 51:01.601
Let me call you back.
Hi. You probably don't remember me.

51:01.768 --> 51:04.938
We met at James Holt's party.
I'm Miranda Priestly's assistant.

51:05.147 --> 51:09.067
The <i>Harry</i> Potter manuscript?
Oh, you're kidding.

51:09.234 --> 51:11.486
<i>Sorry to ask, but I am desperate.</i>

51:11.653 --> 51:15.073
Just tell her it can't be done.
You'll have to come up with a plan B.

51:15.282 --> 51:17.409
This is Miranda Priestly
we're talking about.

51:17.576 --> 51:19.911
There is no plan B.
There's only plan A.

51:20.912 --> 51:22.956
Is she back? Am I fired?

51:23.123 --> 51:26.501
You know, I rarely say this
to people who aren't me...

51:26.668 --> 51:31.173
...but you have got to calm down.
Bloody hell.

51:36.845 --> 51:38.680
Coat, bag.

51:40.640 --> 51:43.018
What's that? Oh, I don't want that.

51:43.185 --> 51:47.939
I'm having lunch with Irv. <i>I'll</i> be back
at 3. I'd like my Starbucks waiting.

51:49.983 --> 51:53.111
And if you don't have
that <i>Harry</i> Potter book by then...

51:53.320 --> 51:55.655
...don't even bother coming back.

52:08.335 --> 52:10.462
Hello?

52:11.296 --> 52:13.089
Quit? Are you sure?

52:13.298 --> 52:17.803
I failed. She's gonna fire me anyway.
I might as well beat her to the punch.

52:18.011 --> 52:21.723
Andy, good for you.
Congratulations. You're free.

52:21.932 --> 52:25.602
- Yeah, well, listen, <i>I'll</i> call you later.
<i>- Okay.</i>

52:26.645 --> 52:29.564
- Hello?
- I'm brilliant. No, really.

52:30.023 --> 52:32.859
<i>Monuments should be
erected in my honor.</i>

52:33.026 --> 52:34.736
- You didn't.
- Oh, yes.

52:34.903 --> 52:39.574
Friend of a friend does the cover art,
and she happens to have the manuscript.

52:40.242 --> 52:45.705
Oh, no, because that would mean
that I actually did something right.

52:45.872 --> 52:47.874
It's just. . ._

52:48.041 --> 52:50.085
The thing is, Christian, I was just--

52:50.293 --> 52:54.673
Look, you want this thing, you better
hurry. I'll meet you at the St. Regis.

53:02.597 --> 53:04.266
Excuse me.

53:14.943 --> 53:17.195
Welcome to the St. Regis.
May I assist you?

53:17.362 --> 53:20.073
Yes, I'm meeting someone
at the King Cole Bar.

53:20.240 --> 53:22.117
Right this way.

53:25.495 --> 53:28.248
- You have one hour.
- Thank you.

53:38.008 --> 53:42.804
One copy. What are my twins
gonna do with that? Share?

53:43.013 --> 53:45.390
Oh, no, I made two copies.
And had them covered...

53:45.557 --> 53:48.351
...reset and bound so they
wouldn't look like manuscripts.

53:48.560 --> 53:52.022
This is an extra copy to have on file,
you know, just in case.

53:52.188 --> 53:55.317
Well, where are these fabulous copies?
I don't see them anywhere.

53:57.861 --> 54:01.364
<i>They're with the twins. You know,
on the train on the way to Grandma's.</i>

54:03.742 --> 54:05.327
Is there anything else
I can do for you?

54:09.623 --> 54:11.166
That's all.

54:11.583 --> 54:12.918
<i>Okay-</i>

54:28.516 --> 54:31.561
- Hey.
- Hey, I went to Dean and DeLuc:a.

54:31.728 --> 54:36.066
Man, they charge, like,
$5 a strawberry there. But I figure...

54:36.399 --> 54:38.443
...since you quit your job...

54:39.027 --> 54:40.570
...we should celebrate.

54:40.987 --> 54:42.364
Listen, Nate...

54:42.781 --> 54:47.577
Wait, you quit your job, but you're still
working on the twins' science project?

54:49.579 --> 54:54.834
- Well, that's big of you.
- Okay, after we talked, I realized...

54:55.043 --> 55:00.006
...it doesn't make sense throwing away
all those months of hard work.

55:00.215 --> 55:02.133
I had a moment of weakness,
that's all.

55:02.300 --> 55:05.887
Yeah, well, either that, or your job sucks
and your boss is a wacko.

55:08.765 --> 55:10.684
All right.

55:11.184 --> 55:14.104
Whatever. It's your job.

55:16.022 --> 55:17.649
Nate.

55:18.316 --> 55:20.193
Come on.

55:20.360 --> 55:22.195
I'm still the same person I was.

55:22.362 --> 55:26.199
I still want the same things. Okay?

55:26.366 --> 55:30.245
I promise. Same Andy. Better clothes.

55:31.663 --> 55:33.498
I liked the old clothes.

55:34.916 --> 55:36.584
Really?

55:37.544 --> 55:40.839
Well, what about these necklaces?
Do you like them?

55:41.464 --> 55:45.677
No? And this dress? It's new.

55:48.680 --> 55:51.349
Well, there is one other thing
that's new...

55:51.516 --> 55:54.602
...that I thought you might like, but...

55:55.895 --> 55:57.272
What about this?

55:59.357 --> 56:02.193
You don't like it,
I should better do the twins'--

56:22.047 --> 56:24.966
Is this number two look?
This is number two?

56:25.592 --> 56:29.596
- Hi.
- Hi. All right, turn around for me, darling.

56:29.804 --> 56:33.099
Oh, I get it. I get it. The piece
is called "Urban Jungle," right?

56:33.266 --> 56:36.478
Yes. The modern woman
unleashes the animal within...

56:36.644 --> 56:38.563
...to take on the big city.

56:38.730 --> 56:40.356
Good. Go.

56:41.274 --> 56:45.403
Sometimes I can't believe I talk about
this crap all day. Bobby, come here.

56:45.570 --> 56:47.530
- Thanks.
- Make sure Miranda gets these...

56:47.697 --> 56:51.493
...as soon as possible. And tell her that I
switched in the Dior for the Rocha.

56:52.869 --> 56:54.913
Great, can't wait.

56:55.080 --> 56:58.291
- Excuse me. Can we adjust the attitude?
- I'm sorry.

56:58.458 --> 57:01.294
Don't make me feed you
to one of the models.

57:01.836 --> 57:05.673
It's a busy day. And my personal life
is hanging by a thread, that's all.

57:05.840 --> 57:10.303
Well, join the club. That happens when
you start doing well at work, darling.

57:10.470 --> 57:12.847
Let me know when your whole life
goes up in smoke.

57:13.014 --> 57:14.891
That means it's time for a promotion.

57:22.482 --> 57:25.485
No. All right, February.
Back of the issue.

57:25.693 --> 57:27.821
Did anybody speak
with Salma's people yet?

57:27.987 --> 57:30.990
Yes. She'd rather do a summer cover,
because she has a movie--

57:31.199 --> 57:35.286
No. Also I'm pulling the Toobin piece
on the Supreme Court women.

57:36.246 --> 57:39.666
Woman. And I need to see a new draft
on that piece about shopping...

57:39.833 --> 57:42.043
...for a plastic surgeon. It's dull.

57:42.794 --> 57:46.589
And this layout for
the "Winter Wonderland" spread...

57:46.756 --> 57:49.134
Not wonderful yet.

57:49.342 --> 57:51.761
- Okay, <i>I'll</i> look at it.
- What about Testino?

57:51.928 --> 57:53.721
- Where are we on that?
- Zac Posen's...

57:53.930 --> 57:56.307
...doing some sculptural suits,
so I suggested...

57:56.474 --> 57:58.893
...that Testino shoot them
at the Noguchi Garden.

57:59.269 --> 58:00.770
Perfect.

58:00.979 --> 58:05.066
Thank God somebody came to work
today. What about accessories for April?

58:05.233 --> 58:09.904
One thought I had was enamel:
bangles, pendants, earrings-

58:10.113 --> 58:12.115
No, we did that two years ago.
What else?

58:12.323 --> 58:15.535
They're showing a lot of florals
right now, so I was thinking I--

58:15.743 --> 58:20.039
Florals? For spring? Groundbreaking.

58:20.248 --> 58:23.835
We thought of shooting them in an
industrial space. The contrast between...

58:24.002 --> 58:27.338
...the feminine florals, and the
rough-hewn background would create...

58:27.547 --> 58:30.049
-...this wonderful tension with-
- No.

58:30.216 --> 58:33.011
Which would...

58:39.684 --> 58:42.729
Does anybody else have
anything I can possibly use?

58:43.646 --> 58:46.649
Antibacterial wipes, perhaps?

58:51.070 --> 58:55.366
- How's the cold doing?
- Like death warmed up, actually.

58:56.993 --> 59:00.538
God. It's the benefit tonight. I've been
looking forward to it for months.

59:00.705 --> 59:04.250
I refuse to be sick. I'm wearing
Valentino, for crying out loud.

59:05.710 --> 59:09.297
Right. Well, everybody will be
leaving soon to get ready...

59:09.464 --> 59:13.426
...so I suggest you go drop Miranda's
Fendi bag off at the showroom...

59:13.593 --> 59:15.303
...then I suppose you can go home.

59:15.511 --> 59:19.224
Yeah? Oh, wow, that is great.

59:19.390 --> 59:22.894
Perfect, actually. I need to get to
Magnolia Bakery before it closes.

59:23.061 --> 59:26.773
It's Nate's birthday tonight. So we're
having a little party for him, and--

59:26.981 --> 59:29.943
Yeah, I'm hearing this:
And I wanna hear this:

59:31.361 --> 59:33.112
Bye.

59:34.656 --> 59:38.201
I love my job,
I love my job, I love my job.

59:46.501 --> 59:48.169
Hello?

59:52.006 --> 59:55.510
Before the benefit tonight,
I need to make sure that you're both...

59:55.677 --> 59:57.720
...fully prepped on the guest list.

59:58.638 --> 01:00:02.684
But I thought that only the first
assistant went to the benefit.

01:00:02.850 --> 01:00:05.561
Only when the first assistant
hasn't decided to become...

01:00:05.728 --> 01:00:08.564
...an incubus of viral plague.

01:00:09.732 --> 01:00:12.318
You'll come and help Emily.

01:00:13.236 --> 01:00:14.570
That's all.

01:00:15.280 --> 01:00:18.074
Right. These are all of the guests.

01:00:18.241 --> 01:00:21.577
Miranda invites everyone. We have
to make sure that they all think...

01:00:21.786 --> 01:00:23.621
...that she knows
exactly who they are.

01:00:23.830 --> 01:00:25.873
And I've been studying for weeks.

01:00:26.082 --> 01:00:30.837
- I have to learn all these by tonight?
- Now, don't be silly, Andrea. These too.

01:00:31.379 --> 01:00:34.090
Better start without me.
I'll get there as soon as I can.

01:00:34.257 --> 01:00:37.135
Andy, come on, it's his birth--

01:00:37.302 --> 01:00:39.345
Okay, but hurry.

01:00:39.554 --> 01:00:42.181
Believe me, I will.
This is the last thing I want to--

01:00:42.390 --> 01:00:46.102
I love that. I'll call you
the second I'm leaving, okay?

01:00:46.602 --> 01:00:48.688
- Will that fit me?
- Oh, yeah.

01:00:48.896 --> 01:00:52.191
A little Crisco and some fishing line,
and we're in business.

01:01:18.885 --> 01:01:21.471
Nothing really. This <i>is--</i>
I mean, really, this is...

01:01:21.637 --> 01:01:25.266
...the social event
of the season, and...

01:01:40.490 --> 01:01:43.868
Oh, my God. Andy, you look so chic.

01:01:44.077 --> 01:01:47.622
Thanks, Em. You look so thin.

01:01:47.830 --> 01:01:49.165
- Do I?
- Yeah.

01:01:49.332 --> 01:01:52.210
It's for Paris. I'm on this new diet.
It's very effective.

01:01:52.377 --> 01:01:55.713
I don't eat anything, and then
when I feel like I'm about to faint...

01:01:55.880 --> 01:01:58.758
-...I eat a cube of cheese.
- Well, it's definitely working.

01:01:58.925 --> 01:02:02.261
I know. I'm just one stomach flu
away from my goal weight.

01:02:18.069 --> 01:02:22.657
That's John Folger, the new artistic
director of the Chelsea Rep.

01:02:22.824 --> 01:02:24.200
- John.
- Hey there.

01:02:24.367 --> 01:02:27.120
- Thanks for coming.
- Thanks. It's always nice seeing you.

01:02:27.328 --> 01:02:29.372
Stop fidgeting.

01:02:29.539 --> 01:02:31.541
I'm sorry. I'm so late.

01:02:31.541 --> 01:02:36.541
Just deal with it. You have to be here.

01:02:39.006 --> 01:02:41.050
Emily. Come here.

01:02:41.217 --> 01:02:43.970
Isn't that Jacqueline Follet
from French <i>Runway?</i>

01:02:44.178 --> 01:02:45.930
Oh, my God, Miranda hates her.

01:02:46.097 --> 01:02:48.266
She was supposed to arrive
after Miranda left.

01:02:48.433 --> 01:02:49.892
- I didn't know.
- Yeah.

01:02:50.309 --> 01:02:53.020
Miranda. Fabulous event, as always.

01:02:53.187 --> 01:02:54.689
You've brought Jacqueline.

01:03:00.194 --> 01:03:04.407
Wonderful. We're so happy that you
were able to come to our little gathering.

01:03:04.574 --> 01:03:07.869
Of course.
I plan my whole year around this.

01:03:08.619 --> 01:03:12.790
Well, we're so grateful that you do.

01:03:14.292 --> 01:03:17.378
- Ciao.
- Have you gotten my note?

01:03:17.545 --> 01:03:18.838
Yes, I did.

01:03:19.005 --> 01:03:21.257
- We'll discuss it on Wednesday.
- Yes, I agree.

01:03:21.424 --> 01:03:23.259
- No business tonight.
- Not tonight.

01:03:23.426 --> 01:03:24.927
<i>EH30'! -</i>

01:03:26.053 --> 01:03:29.724
- Em?
- Oh, great. Thanks.

01:03:34.061 --> 01:03:36.731
Oh... Oh, my God.

01:03:36.898 --> 01:03:39.233
I can't-- I just can't remember
what his name is.

01:03:39.400 --> 01:03:42.445
I saw his name this morning on the list.
It's-- On, I know this.

01:03:42.612 --> 01:03:45.364
It's something to do with-
Wait, he was part of the...

01:03:46.032 --> 01:03:47.575
Oh, God, I know this. It's...

01:03:49.243 --> 01:03:50.870
It's Ambassador Franklin.

01:03:51.037 --> 01:03:53.748
And that's the woman
that he left his wife for, Rebecca.

01:03:56.083 --> 01:03:57.793
Rebecca.

01:03:57.960 --> 01:04:00.505
- Ambassador.
- Miranda, you look fabulous.

01:04:00.671 --> 01:04:03.382
- You're very kind.
- Thank you.

01:04:03.591 --> 01:04:08.137
Welcome back to civilization.
You must be so relieved.

01:04:13.601 --> 01:04:15.144
- Look at you.
- Hello.

01:04:15.311 --> 01:04:18.147
You're-- You're a vision.

01:04:18.314 --> 01:04:20.149
Thank God I saved your job.

01:04:20.316 --> 01:04:24.987
Okay. You know, I figured out
a few things on my own too.

01:04:25.154 --> 01:04:27.573
Turns out, I'm not as nice
as you thought.

01:04:27.740 --> 01:04:28.866
I hope not.

01:04:30.117 --> 01:04:32.286
Wow, if it weren't
for the stupid boyfriend...

01:04:32.453 --> 01:04:35.206
...I'd have to whisk you away
right here and now.

01:04:37.250 --> 01:04:39.752
Do you actually
say things like that to people?

01:04:39.919 --> 01:04:41.712
Evidently.

01:04:41.879 --> 01:04:43.214
Well, I gotta go.

01:04:43.381 --> 01:04:46.551
Are you sure? Because my editor
for New York magazine is inside.

01:04:46.717 --> 01:04:48.636
You know, I could introduce you two.

01:04:49.971 --> 01:04:52.723
You sent over your stuff for me
to look at, I- Remember?

01:04:52.890 --> 01:04:54.559
- Yeah.
- All right, I gotta admit...

01:04:54.725 --> 01:04:58.020
...I only read a couple because
it was a very large packet you sent.

01:04:58.187 --> 01:05:00.064
But what I did read wasn't half bad.

01:05:00.231 --> 01:05:02.733
You know, I think--
I think you have a talent, Andy.

01:05:03.484 --> 01:05:05.695
He should meet you.
Why don't you come in?

01:05:05.861 --> 01:05:07.822
Just for one drink.

01:05:08.030 --> 01:05:11.117
Okay. Yeah, I guess I could for one--

01:05:12.034 --> 01:05:15.371
No, I can't.
I'm sorry, but I have to go.

01:05:15.538 --> 01:05:19.000
All right.
Give my best to the boyfriend.

01:05:26.090 --> 01:05:28.509
Roy, I'm sorry. Can you go any faster?

01:05:28.676 --> 01:05:31.178
I'm sure Nate will understand.

01:05:33.931 --> 01:05:35.349
Yeah.

01:05:38.853 --> 01:05:40.271
Hey.

01:05:55.953 --> 01:05:57.663
Happy birthday.

01:06:01.876 --> 01:06:04.503
Nate, I'm so sorry.

01:06:04.670 --> 01:06:08.799
I kept trying to leave,
but there was a lot going on...

01:06:08.966 --> 01:06:10.968
...and you know
I didn't have a choice.

01:06:11.469 --> 01:06:13.346
Don't worry about it.

01:06:14.722 --> 01:06:16.098
I'm going to bed.

01:06:17.933 --> 01:06:19.477
Can we at least talk about this?

01:06:28.611 --> 01:06:31.030
You look really pretty.

01:07:12.321 --> 01:07:14.490
Andrea?

01:07:26.460 --> 01:07:27.837
Do you have the Book?

01:07:34.885 --> 01:07:38.389
Paris is the most important week
of my entire year.

01:07:38.597 --> 01:07:42.059
I need the best possible team
with me.

01:07:43.060 --> 01:07:45.271
That no longer includes Emily.

01:07:47.648 --> 01:07:50.151
Wait, you-- You want me to--?

01:07:52.153 --> 01:07:56.365
No. Miranda, I-- Emily would die.

01:07:56.574 --> 01:07:59.285
Her whole life is about Paris.

01:07:59.452 --> 01:08:01.579
She hasn't eaten in weeks, I--

01:08:01.746 --> 01:08:06.584
I can't do that, Miranda, I can't.

01:08:06.751 --> 01:08:10.254
If you don't go, I'll assume
you're not serious about your future.

01:08:10.421 --> 01:08:14.759
At <i>Runway</i> or any other publication.

01:08:20.014 --> 01:08:22.349
The decision's yours.

01:08:23.726 --> 01:08:25.978
- But--
- That's all.

01:09:26.705 --> 01:09:29.708
- Hey, Andy.
- Hey.

01:09:29.875 --> 01:09:31.752
You coming to bed anytime soon?

01:09:31.919 --> 01:09:34.380
Yeah, five minutes, okay?

01:10:29.810 --> 01:10:32.021
Andrea, don't forget to tell Emily.

01:10:34.481 --> 01:10:36.650
Do it now.

01:10:46.702 --> 01:10:48.746
Don't pick up.

01:10:48.913 --> 01:10:50.331
Don't pick up. Don't pick up.

01:10:50.497 --> 01:10:51.540
<i>- Don't pick--
- Hi.</i>

01:10:51.707 --> 01:10:53.459
<i>- Emily.
- Hi, hi. Sorry I'm late.</i>

01:10:53.626 --> 01:10:56.170
It's just, Miranda wanted
some scarves from Hermés.

01:10:56.337 --> 01:10:58.839
She did tell me yesterday.
I forgot, like an idiot.

01:10:59.006 --> 01:11:03.093
<i>- So I freaked out, of course.
- Emily- Emily,</i> I <i>need to talk to you.</i>

01:11:03.260 --> 01:11:05.930
I called Martine at home
and she opened the shop early-

01:11:06.096 --> 01:11:09.683
I'm sorry. She opened the shop early
for me, so I got them, which is great.

01:11:09.892 --> 01:11:12.645
Yeah, okay, Emily,
when you come in...

01:11:12.811 --> 01:11:15.230
...there's something
I have to talk to you about.

01:11:15.397 --> 01:11:18.484
<i>- I hope it's not another Miranda problem.
- Not exactly.</i>

01:11:18.651 --> 01:11:21.612
Well, good, because I've got
so much to deal with before I go.

01:11:21.779 --> 01:11:23.405
I swear to God, I mean-

01:11:27.576 --> 01:11:28.994
Oh, my God!

01:11:29.620 --> 01:11:30.955
Emily?

01:11:40.255 --> 01:11:44.259
I don't care if she was gonna fire you
or beat you with a red-hot poker...

01:11:44.426 --> 01:11:45.844
...you should have said no.

01:11:46.011 --> 01:11:49.682
Emily, I didn't have a choice.
You know how she is.

01:11:49.848 --> 01:11:52.810
Please, that is a pathetic excuse.

01:11:56.522 --> 01:11:58.065
Thanks.

01:11:59.233 --> 01:12:04.029
Do you know what really just gets me
about this whole thing?

01:12:04.196 --> 01:12:06.407
Is that, you know,
you're the one who said...

01:12:06.573 --> 01:12:08.909
...that you don't really care
about this stuff.

01:12:09.076 --> 01:12:12.413
You don't really care about fashion,
you just wanna be a journalist.

01:12:12.579 --> 01:12:14.373
Oh, what a pile of bollocks!

01:12:14.540 --> 01:12:16.542
I know you're mad,
I don't blame you.

01:12:16.709 --> 01:12:20.754
Face it, Andy, you sold your soul the day
you put on that pair of Jimmy Choos.

01:12:20.921 --> 01:12:25.509
I saw it. And do you know what really
just kills me about this whole thing?

01:12:25.676 --> 01:12:30.472
Is the clothes that you're gonna get,
I mean, you don't deserve them.

01:12:30.639 --> 01:12:33.475
You eat carbs, for chrissake!

01:12:33.809 --> 01:12:35.269
God!

01:12:35.436 --> 01:12:37.604
It's so unfair.

01:12:38.105 --> 01:12:40.315
- Emily...
- Just go.

01:12:46.572 --> 01:12:49.408
- Emily, I--
- I said, go.

01:12:54.913 --> 01:12:56.915
You are going to Paris
for the couture shows?

01:12:57.082 --> 01:12:59.209
That's the coolest fashion event
of the year.

01:12:59.960 --> 01:13:02.504
- Who are you gonna see, Galliano?
- Yeah.

01:13:02.671 --> 01:13:04.256
- And Lagerfeld?
- Yep.

01:13:04.423 --> 01:13:08.177
- And Nicolas Ghesquiére.
- Ye-— Okay, now you're scaring me.

01:13:08.343 --> 01:13:10.471
- Hey-
- Hey-

01:13:10.637 --> 01:13:14.391
This show is amazing.
I am so proud of you.

01:13:14.558 --> 01:13:15.642
Thank you.

01:13:15.809 --> 01:13:18.520
Start with the photos in the back,
work your way forward.

01:13:18.687 --> 01:13:21.106
The way I designed it.
Brilliant. You will love it.

01:13:21.273 --> 01:13:23.150
- Of course.
- And you...

01:13:23.317 --> 01:13:25.110
...I have somebody
I want you to meet.

01:13:25.277 --> 01:13:26.695
Art and sex. Lead the way.

01:13:26.862 --> 01:13:29.031
- See you later.
- Okay.

01:13:47.800 --> 01:13:49.676
Hey.

01:13:49.843 --> 01:13:51.970
Hey, Miranda girl.

01:13:53.555 --> 01:13:55.182
Hi.

01:13:55.349 --> 01:13:56.975
I was just thinking about you.

01:13:57.142 --> 01:13:58.977
Oh, come on.

01:13:59.186 --> 01:14:00.521
- It's true.
- No.

01:14:00.687 --> 01:14:03.148
I'm profiling Gaultier for Interview.

01:14:03.315 --> 01:14:05.484
And making my Paris plans...

01:14:05.651 --> 01:14:10.114
...I found myself wondering
if you were gonna be there.

01:14:10.280 --> 01:14:15.410
Well, actually, I am going.

01:14:15.577 --> 01:14:17.037
Great.

01:14:17.204 --> 01:14:20.415
I'm staying at a fantastic little hotel
in the seventh.

01:14:20.582 --> 01:14:24.294
Right across the street from a falafel
restaurant that will change your life.

01:14:26.255 --> 01:14:29.341
I'm sorry, I'll be too busy working.

01:14:29.508 --> 01:14:32.094
You'll have to find
someone else's life to change.

01:14:33.595 --> 01:14:35.722
Well, that's just it.

01:14:35.889 --> 01:14:38.517
I'm beginning to wonder if I can.

01:14:51.446 --> 01:14:52.739
Lily-

01:14:54.116 --> 01:14:56.118
Lily, he's just a guy
I know from work.

01:14:56.285 --> 01:14:59.329
- Yeah, that looked like work.
- You're making a big deal out of-

01:14:59.496 --> 01:15:02.791
You know, the Andy I know
is madly in love with Nate...

01:15:03.417 --> 01:15:05.127
...is always five minutes early...

01:15:05.294 --> 01:15:07.921
...and thinks, I don't know,
Club Monaco is couture.

01:15:08.547 --> 01:15:11.550
For the last 16 years,
I've known everything about that Andy.

01:15:11.717 --> 01:15:13.051
But this person?

01:15:13.218 --> 01:15:15.512
This glamazon
who skulks around in corners...

01:15:15.679 --> 01:15:17.472
...with some random,
hot fashion guy?

01:15:18.807 --> 01:15:20.976
I don't get her.

01:15:21.852 --> 01:15:24.563
- Lily.
- Have fun in Paris.

01:15:25.939 --> 01:15:27.858
You're going to Paris?

01:15:28.901 --> 01:15:30.819
Yeah, it just happened.

01:15:31.612 --> 01:15:34.406
I thought Paris was a big deal
for Emily or--

01:15:34.907 --> 01:15:37.367
Great. Now you're gonna
give me a hard time too?

01:15:39.328 --> 01:15:40.913
Hey, Andy.

01:15:41.079 --> 01:15:42.706
Andy!

01:15:42.873 --> 01:15:45.918
- Andy, what the hell is wrong with you?
- I didn't have a choice.

01:15:46.084 --> 01:15:48.253
- Miranda asked me. I couldn't say no.
- I know.

01:15:48.420 --> 01:15:50.923
Your answer for everything:
"I didn't have a choice."

01:15:51.089 --> 01:15:54.218
Like this job was forced on you,
like you don't make decisions.

01:15:54.384 --> 01:15:58.180
You're mad because I work late and
I missed your birthday party. I'm sorry.

01:15:58.347 --> 01:16:02.309
- Oh, come on, what am I, 4?
- You-— You hate Runway. And Miranda.

01:16:02.476 --> 01:16:05.437
And you think fashion is stupid.
You've made that clear.

01:16:05.604 --> 01:16:08.649
Andy, I make
port-wine reductions all day.

01:16:08.815 --> 01:16:10.734
I'm not exactly in the Peace Corps.

01:16:10.901 --> 01:16:14.112
You know, lwouldn't care
if you were out pole-dancing all night...

01:16:14.279 --> 01:16:16.740
...as long as you did it
with a little integrity.

01:16:16.907 --> 01:16:18.617
You used to say this was just a job.

01:16:18.784 --> 01:16:20.786
You used to make fun
of the <i>Runway</i> girls.

01:16:20.953 --> 01:16:23.121
What happened?
Now you've become one of them.

01:16:24.456 --> 01:16:26.833
- That's absurd.
- Hey, that's okay, that's fine.

01:16:27.000 --> 01:16:28.377
Just own up to it.

01:16:28.543 --> 01:16:32.256
And then we can stop pretending like
we have anything in common anymore.

01:16:32.839 --> 01:16:36.051
- You don't mean that, you-—
- No,ldo.

01:16:43.016 --> 01:16:47.104
Well, maybe this trip
is coming at a good time.

01:16:47.271 --> 01:16:49.690
Maybe we should take a break.

01:16:57.155 --> 01:16:58.615
Nate?

01:17:08.333 --> 01:17:12.004
I'm sorry. Just one second.

01:17:14.006 --> 01:17:16.133
You know, in case
you were wondering...

01:17:16.300 --> 01:17:18.427
...the person whose calls
you always take...

01:17:18.593 --> 01:17:20.429
...that's the relationship you're in.

01:17:20.595 --> 01:17:23.348
I hope you two
are very happy together.

01:17:31.648 --> 01:17:33.942
Hello, Miranda.

01:18:48.183 --> 01:18:49.309
Miranda.

01:18:52.479 --> 01:18:55.357
How are you? So glad to see you.
Thank you for coming.

01:18:55.565 --> 01:18:58.026
- Do you like the collection?
- Absolutely.

01:18:58.193 --> 01:19:00.946
This is very important.
Very, very important.

01:19:01.488 --> 01:19:02.948
This is my new Emily.

01:19:03.115 --> 01:19:04.324
Hello. How do you do?

01:19:04.491 --> 01:19:06.076
- I'm good.
- Nice to meet you.

01:19:06.243 --> 01:19:07.869
- A pleasure.
- You love the show?

01:19:13.583 --> 01:19:16.545
- Miranda. This way, please.
- This way.

01:19:22.008 --> 01:19:25.011
Miranda. Nigel.
Fashion's great gatekeepers.

01:19:25.178 --> 01:19:30.183
Miranda, what is Runway's position on
French fashion versus American fashion?

01:19:31.059 --> 01:19:34.521
I've been thinking.
You still owe me for <i>Harry</i> Potter.

01:19:34.688 --> 01:19:36.565
- Oh, do I?
- Of course you do.

01:19:36.731 --> 01:19:38.650
Are you working tonight?

01:19:40.026 --> 01:19:43.238
- No, actually, Miranda has a dinner.
- Great, you're free.

01:19:43.447 --> 01:19:46.324
Oh, but there is the problem
of le boyfriend.

01:19:47.659 --> 01:19:50.370
Wait, don't tell me,
the boyfriend non <i>plus?</i>

01:19:52.622 --> 01:19:55.250
Oh, you're so full of it.
You're not <i>desolé</i> at all.

01:19:55.417 --> 01:19:57.919
Not even a little.
What time should I pick you up?

01:19:59.963 --> 01:20:01.214
I'll call you.

01:20:01.756 --> 01:20:03.800
Christian, photo!

01:20:25.322 --> 01:20:27.741
Oh, there you are.

01:20:29.034 --> 01:20:34.289
We need to go over the seating chart.

01:20:34.498 --> 01:20:38.043
- For the luncheon.
- Okay. Yeah, sure.

01:20:38.210 --> 01:20:41.129
I have it right here.

01:20:44.382 --> 01:20:46.718
By all means, move at a glacial pace.

01:20:46.885 --> 01:20:48.762
You know how that thrills me.

01:20:56.269 --> 01:21:00.398
Okay. So...

01:21:01.274 --> 01:21:07.072
...first of all, we need to move
Snoop Dogg to my table.

01:21:07.239 --> 01:21:08.657
But your table's full.

01:21:10.450 --> 01:21:12.160
Stephen isn't coming.

01:21:12.869 --> 01:21:15.163
Oh, Stephen is--

01:21:15.330 --> 01:21:19.251
So I don't need to fetch Stephen
from the airport tomorrow?

01:21:19.918 --> 01:21:23.630
Well, if you speak to him
and he decides to rethink the divorce...

01:21:23.797 --> 01:21:26.258
...then yes, fetch away.

01:21:26.925 --> 01:21:31.012
You're very fetching, so go fetch.

01:21:36.142 --> 01:21:42.440
And then, when we get back to
New York, we need to contact Leslie...

01:21:43.066 --> 01:21:48.405
...and see what she can do
to minimize the press on all this.

01:21:51.866 --> 01:21:54.286
Another divorce.

01:21:54.452 --> 01:21:57.497
Splashed across "Page Six."

01:21:57.706 --> 01:22:00.709
I can just imagine
what they're gonna write about me:

01:22:00.875 --> 01:22:04.796
"The Dragon Lady. Career-obsessed.

01:22:04.963 --> 01:22:08.508
Snow Queen drives away
another Mr. Priestly."

01:22:09.676 --> 01:22:14.889
Rupert Murdoch should cut me a check
for all the papers I sell for him.

01:22:16.850 --> 01:22:19.019
Anyway, I don't--

01:22:19.185 --> 01:22:22.689
I don't really care
what anybody writes about me.

01:22:24.774 --> 01:22:30.113
But my-- My girls, I just--
It's just so unfair to the girls.

01:22:30.280 --> 01:22:32.741
And it's just...

01:22:35.493 --> 01:22:37.245
...another disappointment.

01:22:37.412 --> 01:22:41.166
Another letdown.
Another father. Figure.

01:22:42.167 --> 01:22:43.960
Gone.

01:22:45.462 --> 01:22:48.173
Anyway, the point is...

01:22:49.633 --> 01:22:51.509
The point is...

01:22:53.345 --> 01:22:57.515
The point is, we really need to figure out
where to place Donatella...

01:22:57.682 --> 01:23:00.977
...because she's barely
speaking to anyone.

01:23:10.612 --> 01:23:13.239
I'm so sorry, Miranda.

01:23:13.406 --> 01:23:15.867
If you want me
to cancel your evening, I can.

01:23:16.076 --> 01:23:19.204
Don't be ridiculous.
Why would we do that?

01:23:22.874 --> 01:23:24.709
Is there anything else I can do?

01:23:26.294 --> 01:23:28.213
Your job.

01:23:31.257 --> 01:23:33.093
That's all.

01:23:59.369 --> 01:24:01.705
Hi. I need Miranda's itinerary
for tomorrow.

01:24:01.871 --> 01:24:03.456
- Okay. Come in.
- All right.

01:24:08.336 --> 01:24:09.796
Who put that together for you?

01:24:11.005 --> 01:24:14.259
Oh, this isn't--
It's just something I threw on.

01:24:14.426 --> 01:24:17.345
Turn around. Let me see. Turn.

01:24:21.015 --> 01:24:23.852
- It's really just-- No, it's- No.
- Yeah? Yeah? Okay, good.

01:24:24.018 --> 01:24:27.397
Gorgeous. Really.
I think that my work here is done.

01:24:29.983 --> 01:24:32.777
We're going to celebrate.
I'm going to get some champagne.

01:24:32.944 --> 01:24:34.571
Okay. What are we toasting?

01:24:34.738 --> 01:24:39.576
We're toasting, my dear,
to the dream job.

01:24:39.743 --> 01:24:42.871
The one that a million girls wanted.

01:24:43.037 --> 01:24:44.956
Which I got months ago.

01:24:46.332 --> 01:24:48.793
I'm not talking about you.

01:24:51.796 --> 01:24:54.257
- James Holt.
- Yeah.

01:24:54.424 --> 01:25:00.638
Massimo Corteleoni is investing
in James' company and taking it global.

01:25:00.805 --> 01:25:04.309
Bags, shoes, fragrances, the works.

01:25:05.268 --> 01:25:08.730
And James needs a partner.

01:25:08.897 --> 01:25:14.652
And that partner would be me.

01:25:16.905 --> 01:25:18.698
- Does Miranda-—?
- No, Miranda knows...

01:25:18.865 --> 01:25:21.826
...because she put me up for it.
Oh, God, no. Can you imagine?

01:25:22.243 --> 01:25:24.329
But-- But-- But you're leaving.

01:25:25.580 --> 01:25:28.875
- I can't imagine <i>Runway</i> without you.
- I know.

01:25:29.042 --> 01:25:32.587
I'm so excited, though!
For the first time in 18 years...

01:25:32.670 --> 01:25:34.839
...I'll call the shots in my own life.

01:25:34.923 --> 01:25:37.300
Oh, my God!

01:25:37.467 --> 01:25:42.180
I'm going to be able to come to Paris
and actually see Paris.

01:25:44.682 --> 01:25:47.644
Well, congratulations.

01:25:47.811 --> 01:25:50.647
Nigel, you deserve it.

01:25:52.607 --> 01:25:55.109
You bet your size-six ass.

01:25:56.194 --> 01:25:59.864
- Four.
- Really?

01:26:00.031 --> 01:26:03.785
- Cheers.
- Cheers to you.

01:26:03.952 --> 01:26:07.080
- To us.
- Let me see that.

01:26:10.959 --> 01:26:12.627
Okay, I just wanna say that, yes...

01:26:12.794 --> 01:26:15.713
...there are things Miranda does
that I don't agree with-

01:26:15.880 --> 01:26:17.882
Come on, you hate her.
Just admit it to me.

01:26:18.049 --> 01:26:20.927
- No.
- She's a notorious sadist.

01:26:21.094 --> 01:26:23.221
And not- Not in a good way.

01:26:23.429 --> 01:26:26.391
Okay, she's tough.
But if Miranda were a man...

01:26:26.558 --> 01:26:30.270
...no one would notice anything about
her except how great she is at her job.

01:26:31.980 --> 01:26:34.065
I'm sorry, I can't- I can't believe this.

01:26:34.232 --> 01:26:36.276
- You're defending her?
- Yeah.

01:26:36.442 --> 01:26:39.821
The wide-eyed girl,
peddling her earnest newspaper stories?

01:26:40.446 --> 01:26:43.074
You, my friend,
are crossing over to the dark side.

01:26:45.243 --> 01:26:46.619
I resent that.

01:26:46.786 --> 01:26:49.873
- You shouldn't. It's sexy.
- Sexy?

01:26:52.834 --> 01:26:55.879
- Really?
- Really.

01:27:01.050 --> 01:27:03.636
So do you--? Do you know
where we're going? Because...

01:27:03.803 --> 01:27:04.846
- Yeah.
-...I'm lost.

01:27:05.013 --> 01:27:07.640
Don't worry. I know this city
like the back of my hand.

01:27:07.807 --> 01:27:10.268
It's my favorite place
in the whole world.

01:27:10.435 --> 01:27:12.604
You know, Gertrude Stein once said:

01:27:12.770 --> 01:27:17.066
"America is my country,
and Paris is my hometown."

01:27:18.443 --> 01:27:20.361
It's true.

01:27:20.528 --> 01:27:23.364
What do you do?
Do you just write stuff like that down...

01:27:23.531 --> 01:27:26.993
...and then file it away
to use on us girls?

01:27:27.160 --> 01:27:28.953
I'm Christian Thompson.
That's my way.

01:27:29.120 --> 01:27:30.538
That's your way. Right.

01:27:30.705 --> 01:27:33.374
I work freelance.
I have a lot of free time on my hands.

01:27:35.251 --> 01:27:37.837
You know, I never understood...

01:27:38.004 --> 01:27:41.007
...why everyone
was so crazy about Paris.

01:27:41.174 --> 01:27:47.138
But it is so beautiful.

01:27:50.308 --> 01:27:54.479
I can't. I'm sorry, I can't, I--

01:27:54.687 --> 01:27:58.441
You know, Nate and I just split up
a couple of days ago, and I can't--

01:28:02.445 --> 01:28:05.740
I've had too much wine
and my hearing-- Vision--

01:28:05.907 --> 01:28:08.242
Judgment's impaired.

01:28:10.870 --> 01:28:15.083
No, I barely know you.
I'm in a strange city.

01:28:16.042 --> 01:28:19.921
I am out of excuses.

01:28:20.380 --> 01:28:21.756
Thank God.

01:29:10.263 --> 01:29:12.432
Yes.

01:29:27.864 --> 01:29:30.616
Oh, hi. What the hell is this?

01:29:30.783 --> 01:29:33.953
What does it look like? It's a mockup.

01:29:34.454 --> 01:29:36.164
Yeah. Of...?

01:29:36.330 --> 01:29:38.249
Of what American <i>Runway</i>
will look like...

01:29:38.416 --> 01:29:41.419
...when Jacqueline Follet
is the new editor in chief.

01:29:43.129 --> 01:29:44.630
They're replacing Miranda?

01:29:44.797 --> 01:29:48.509
Yeah. And she's bringing me in
to run all the editorial content.

01:29:50.887 --> 01:29:52.889
You're really surprised?

01:29:53.056 --> 01:29:56.934
Jacqueline's a lot younger than Miranda.
She has a fresher take on things.

01:29:57.643 --> 01:30:01.189
Not to mention that American Runway
is one of the most expensive books...

01:30:01.355 --> 01:30:02.690
...in the business.

01:30:02.857 --> 01:30:06.652
Jacqueline does the same thing
for a lot less money.

01:30:06.819 --> 01:30:10.323
And lrv's a businessman, you know.

01:30:10.823 --> 01:30:13.659
Miranda will be devastated.
Her whole life is about Runway.

01:30:13.826 --> 01:30:15.536
- He can't do that to her.
- It's done.

01:30:15.703 --> 01:30:18.289
Irv's gonna tell Miranda
after the party for James.

01:30:18.956 --> 01:30:20.416
And she has no idea?

01:30:20.917 --> 01:30:23.002
She's a big girl. She'll be fine.

01:30:26.005 --> 01:30:27.340
I have to go.

01:30:27.507 --> 01:30:31.344
Andy. Andy, it's done.

01:30:32.637 --> 01:30:33.971
Baby, it's done.

01:30:35.389 --> 01:30:37.642
I'm not your baby.

01:30:49.320 --> 01:30:52.365
- Oh, thank God. You're there.
- Excuse me?

01:30:52.532 --> 01:30:56.119
<i>I need to talk to you right away.
It's about Jacqueline Follet. She's--</i>

01:30:57.078 --> 01:31:00.790
Damn. Shit, shit, shit.

01:31:16.889 --> 01:31:18.224
- Yes?
- Oh, hello.

01:31:18.391 --> 01:31:21.310
Mr. Ravitz, I'm so sorry to bother you,
but I was wondering--

01:31:21.477 --> 01:31:23.729
Have you completely lost your mind?

01:31:23.896 --> 01:31:25.481
I need to talk to you.

01:31:25.648 --> 01:31:31.112
- Do not disturb me again.
- But-- It's just-- Miranda!

01:31:48.880 --> 01:31:50.214
Miranda?

01:31:50.381 --> 01:31:53.050
Miranda. Wait, I need to talk to you.

01:31:53.217 --> 01:31:56.179
Irv is making Jacqueline Follet
the editor in chief of <i>Runway.</i>

01:31:56.345 --> 01:31:58.347
Christian told me
he's gonna work for her.

01:31:58.514 --> 01:32:01.934
Irv is gonna tell you today. I thought
if I told you, you could fix it.

01:32:02.101 --> 01:32:04.645
- Do I smell freesias?
- What?

01:32:04.812 --> 01:32:07.940
No. I specifically told them-—

01:32:08.107 --> 01:32:11.903
If I see freesias anywhere...

01:32:11.986 --> 01:32:14.530
...I will be very disappointed.

01:32:15.573 --> 01:32:20.077
For 72 years, <i>Runway</i>
has been more than a magazine.

01:32:20.244 --> 01:32:23.831
It has been a beacon
of elegance and grace.

01:32:23.998 --> 01:32:29.295
Miranda Priestly is the finest
possible guardian of that beacon.

01:32:29.837 --> 01:32:34.717
Setting a standard
that inspires people across the globe.

01:32:34.884 --> 01:32:38.638
Ladies and gentlemen,
I give you Miranda Priestly.

01:32:56.489 --> 01:32:59.075
Thank you, my dear friend.

01:33:03.120 --> 01:33:06.290
Thank you very much
for coming today...

01:33:06.457 --> 01:33:10.836
...to help celebrate
our dear friend, James Holt.

01:33:18.636 --> 01:33:24.809
But before I talk to you about James
and his many accomplishments...

01:33:25.977 --> 01:33:29.855
...I would like first
to share some news with you.

01:33:32.984 --> 01:33:37.822
As many of you know,
recently Massimo Corteleoni...

01:33:37.989 --> 01:33:41.993
...has agreed to finance
the expansion of the James Holt label.

01:33:42.159 --> 01:33:46.038
Transforming the work
of this visionary artist...

01:33:46.205 --> 01:33:50.584
...into a global brand,
which is really an exciting enterprise.

01:33:51.168 --> 01:33:54.130
<i>Runway</i> and James Holt
share many things in common.

01:33:54.297 --> 01:33:59.051
Chief among them,
a commitment to excellence.

01:33:59.218 --> 01:34:02.638
And so it should come as no surprise...

01:34:02.805 --> 01:34:06.100
...that when the time came
for James to choose the new president...

01:34:06.267 --> 01:34:07.935
...of James Holt International...

01:34:08.102 --> 01:34:11.647
...he chose from within
the <i>Runway</i> family.

01:34:12.815 --> 01:34:16.986
And it's my great happiness today
to announce to you all...

01:34:17.153 --> 01:34:21.949
...that that person is my friend...

01:34:22.116 --> 01:34:26.954
...and long-time esteemed colleague,
Jacqueline Follet.

01:34:58.944 --> 01:35:04.658
And now to the main event:
Our celebration of James Holt.

01:35:05.409 --> 01:35:09.121
We at <i>Runway</i> are very proud
to have been among the first to...

01:35:09.288 --> 01:35:12.291
When the time is right
she'll pay me back.

01:35:14.710 --> 01:35:17.046
You sure about that?

01:35:17.213 --> 01:35:18.798
No.

01:35:19.632 --> 01:35:21.926
But I hope for the best.

01:35:22.802 --> 01:35:24.845
I have to.

01:35:44.323 --> 01:35:47.076
You thought I didn't know.

01:35:48.452 --> 01:35:52.123
I've known what was happening
for quite some time.

01:35:53.207 --> 01:35:57.795
It just took me a little while to find
a suitable alternative for Jacqueline.

01:35:58.462 --> 01:36:03.008
And that James Holt job
was just so absurdly overpaid...

01:36:03.175 --> 01:36:06.095
...that of course she jumped at it.

01:36:06.887 --> 01:36:10.349
So I just had to tell Irv
that Jacqueline was unavailable.

01:36:11.058 --> 01:36:14.937
Truth is, there is no one
that can do what I do.

01:36:15.104 --> 01:36:17.398
Including her.

01:36:17.940 --> 01:36:21.235
Any of the other choices
would have found that job impossible...

01:36:21.402 --> 01:36:24.488
...and the magazine
would have suffered.

01:36:25.531 --> 01:36:27.450
Especially because of the list.

01:36:28.993 --> 01:36:33.956
The list of designers, photographers,
editors, writers, models...

01:36:34.123 --> 01:36:36.500
...all of whom were found by me,
nurtured by me...

01:36:36.667 --> 01:36:39.545
...and have promised me
they will follow me...

01:36:39.712 --> 01:36:42.631
...whenever and if ever
I choose to leave <i>Runway.</i>

01:36:45.092 --> 01:36:46.844
So he reconsidered.

01:36:50.639 --> 01:36:56.937
But I was very, very impressed
by how intently you tried to warn me.

01:36:57.104 --> 01:37:02.568
I never thought I would say this,
Andrea, but I really...

01:37:04.069 --> 01:37:06.155
I see a great deal of myself in you.

01:37:09.700 --> 01:37:13.496
You can see beyond what people want,
and what they need...

01:37:13.662 --> 01:37:17.333
...and you can choose for yourself.

01:37:19.960 --> 01:37:23.005
I don't think I'm like that.

01:37:28.636 --> 01:37:32.097
I couldn't do what you did to Nigel.
I couldn't do something like that.

01:37:35.142 --> 01:37:37.019
You already did.

01:37:41.482 --> 01:37:42.816
To Emily.

01:37:43.567 --> 01:37:45.861
That's not what I--

01:37:46.862 --> 01:37:49.365
No, that was different.
I didn't have a choice.

01:37:49.532 --> 01:37:51.075
Oh, no, you chose.

01:37:51.242 --> 01:37:53.244
You chose to get ahead.

01:37:54.245 --> 01:37:57.456
You want this life,
those choices are necessary.

01:37:57.998 --> 01:38:02.169
But what if this isn't what I want?

01:38:02.753 --> 01:38:05.965
I mean, what if I don't wanna live
the way you live?

01:38:06.131 --> 01:38:09.802
Oh, don't be ridiculous, Andrea.
Everybody wants this.

01:38:11.929 --> 01:38:15.516
Everybody wants to be us.

01:39:41.185 --> 01:39:44.355
I have to be at work in 20 minutes.

01:39:45.189 --> 01:39:46.523
What's up?

01:39:48.067 --> 01:39:50.944
Well, I just...

01:39:51.403 --> 01:39:55.407
I wanted to say
that you were right about everything.

01:39:55.699 --> 01:39:57.493
That...

01:39:57.660 --> 01:40:01.038
...I turned my back on my friends
and my family...

01:40:01.205 --> 01:40:04.249
...and on everything
I believed in and...

01:40:04.416 --> 01:40:07.836
- And for what?
- For shoes.

01:40:08.003 --> 01:40:10.756
And shirts.
And jackets and belts and-

01:40:10.923 --> 01:40:12.841
Nate...

01:40:16.553 --> 01:40:18.222
...I'm sorry.

01:40:28.607 --> 01:40:30.818
I flew up to Boston
while you were gone.

01:40:31.860 --> 01:40:33.529
Interviewed at the Oak Room.

01:40:34.738 --> 01:40:36.073
And?

01:40:37.408 --> 01:40:40.160
And you're looking at
their new sous-chef.

01:40:40.327 --> 01:40:44.081
- I'm moving up there in a couple weeks.
- Oh, that's great. Congratulations.

01:40:49.461 --> 01:40:52.965
Don't know what I'm gonna do without
late-night grilled cheeses, but...

01:40:53.674 --> 01:40:57.177
I'm pretty sure
they have bread in Boston.

01:40:57.344 --> 01:41:00.347
May even have Jarlsberg.

01:41:02.766 --> 01:41:04.977
We might be able
to figure something out.

01:41:07.271 --> 01:41:09.064
You think?

01:41:09.606 --> 01:41:11.400
Yeah.

01:41:17.698 --> 01:41:21.535
So, what about you?
I mean, what are you gonna do now?

01:41:21.702 --> 01:41:24.997
I actually-—
I have a job interview today.

01:41:25.164 --> 01:41:26.874
Oh, yeah?

01:41:27.499 --> 01:41:28.834
That's what you're wearing?

01:41:29.752 --> 01:41:32.546
Shut up. I like this.

01:41:37.050 --> 01:41:38.385
Andy. Greg Hill.

01:41:38.552 --> 01:41:39.970
- Hello.
- Come on.

01:41:40.137 --> 01:41:41.472
<i>These clips are excellent.</i>

01:41:41.638 --> 01:41:44.475
This janitors' union thing,
that's exactly what we do here.

01:41:44.641 --> 01:41:48.353
My only question is: <i>Runway?</i>

01:41:48.520 --> 01:41:52.316
You were there for less than a year.
What the hell kind of a blip is that?

01:41:53.734 --> 01:41:56.111
Learned a lot.

01:41:57.529 --> 01:42:01.950
In the end, though,
I kind of screwed it up.

01:42:02.117 --> 01:42:06.121
I called over there for a reference,
left word with some snooty girl...

01:42:06.288 --> 01:42:09.792
...next thing you know, I got a fax
from Miranda Priestly herself...

01:42:09.958 --> 01:42:12.294
...saying of all the assistants
she's ever had...

01:42:12.461 --> 01:42:14.713
...you were by far
her biggest disappointment.

01:42:15.672 --> 01:42:21.011
And if I don't hire you, I am an idiot.

01:42:22.513 --> 01:42:25.015
You must have done something right.

01:42:57.548 --> 01:42:59.091
Miranda Priestly's office.

01:42:59.258 --> 01:43:00.843
Hey, Emily, it's Andy.

01:43:01.009 --> 01:43:02.344
<i>Don't hang up.</i>

01:43:02.511 --> 01:43:04.429
<i>I have a favor to ask you.</i>

01:43:04.596 --> 01:43:07.266
- You have a favor to ask of me?
- Yeah.

01:43:07.432 --> 01:43:10.477
Thing is,
I have all these clothes from Paris...

01:43:10.644 --> 01:43:13.730
...and I don't have any place
to wear them...

01:43:13.897 --> 01:43:16.817
...so I was wondering
if you could take them off my hands.

01:43:21.071 --> 01:43:22.406
Well, I don't know.

01:43:22.573 --> 01:43:26.785
It's a huge imposition,
and I'll have to get them taken in.

01:43:26.952 --> 01:43:29.621
I mean, they'll drown me.

01:43:29.788 --> 01:43:34.167
But I suppose I could help you out.
I'll have Roy pick them up this afternoon.

01:43:34.334 --> 01:43:36.795
Thanks, Em, I appreciate it.

01:43:37.504 --> 01:43:38.839
Good luck.

01:43:48.932 --> 01:43:51.685
You have some very large shoes to fill.

01:43:53.020 --> 01:43:55.188
Hope you know that.

01:44:00.903 --> 01:44:04.072
I don't understand
why it's so challenging...

01:44:04.239 --> 01:44:08.744
...to get my car when I ask for it.

01:44:53.622 --> 01:44:55.666
Go.
